{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793094372679,"sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","part":{"partID":"prt_17cc0c77d001MHejciLJKYNNOK","sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","messageID":"msg_17cc0b9a7001rZJNdVAycSyQdm","type":"tool","id":"call_469a065b71beb993a39aa1a8","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml","offset":751,"limit":700},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml, lines 751-1450\n751:           bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"config_warning\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"field\":\"minIterations\",\"configured\":{min_iterations_raw},\"effective\":{effective_min_iterations},\"maxIterations\":{max_iterations},\"message\":\"minIterations exceeds maxIterations; clamping to the hard cap.\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n752:           log: \"minIterations exceeds maxIterations; clamping to the hard cap.\"\n753:         if_convergence_mode_invalid:\n754:           bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"config_warning\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"field\":\"convergenceMode\",\"fallback\":\"default\",\"message\":\"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n755:           log: \"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\"\n756: \n757:       step_graph_convergence:\n758:         action: \"Evaluate coverage-graph convergence before the inline 3-signal vote and persist the graph decision snapshot\"\n759:         bash: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"research\" --session-id \"{config.lineage.sessionId}\" --convergence-mode \"{convergence_mode}\" --persist-snapshot --iteration \"{current_iteration}\"'\n760:         note: \"Run before the inline vote. STOP from the inline 3-signal vote is allowed only when the graph decision is STOP_ALLOWED or absent.\"\n761:         outputs:\n762:           - graph_decision: \"Tool decision value (CONTINUE | STOP_ALLOWED | STOP_BLOCKED), else null when unavailable\"\n763:           - graph_decision_json: \"JSON-encoded graph decision string, else null\"\n764:           - graph_signals_json: \"Tool signals object, else {}\"\n765:           - graph_blockers_json: \"Tool blockers array, else []\"\n766:           - graph_trace_json: \"Tool trace payload, else []\"\n767:           - graph_convergence_score: \"signals.blendedScore when present, else the best available graph score, else 0\"\n768:         bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"graph_convergence\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"decision\":{graph_decision_json},\"signals\":{graph_signals_json},\"blockers\":{graph_blockers_json},\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n769: \n770:       step_check_convergence:\n771:         action: \"Evaluate stop conditions and combine the inline 3-signal vote with graph convergence\"\n772:         algorithm: |\n773:           1. if iteration_count >= max_iterations: STOP (maxIterationsReached). This terminal cap bypasses quality-guard overrides; record failed guards/blockers as synthesis evidence instead of continuing.\n774:           2. if stuck_count >= config.stuckThreshold: STUCK_RECOVERY\n775:           3. if convergence_mode == \"off\": skip convergence stop candidates and continue unless a terminal cap, pause sentinel, or recovery halt has already fired.\n776:           3a. if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: steps 4 and 5 are telemetry only and cannot set STOP or BLOCKED. Record weighted_stop_score for diagnostics, keep decision = \"CONTINUE\" and choose a broader next focus.\n777:           4. if remaining_questions == 0: STOP (all_questions_answered)\n778:           5. GRAPH-ASSISTED COMPOSITE CONVERGENCE:\n779:                step_graph_convergence already recorded graph_decision, graph_signals_json, graph_blockers_json, and graph_convergence_score for this run.\n780:                The existing inline 3-signal vote still computes the inline STOP candidate and is not replaced.\n781:                signals = []\n782:                Filter: exclude iterations where status == thought from signal inputs (use only evidence iterations)\n783:                a) Rolling average (w=0.30, needs 3+ iterations):\n784:                   avg = mean(last 3 newInfoRatios)\n785:                   stop if avg < convergence_threshold\n786:                b) MAD noise floor (w=0.35, needs 4+ iterations):\n787:                   noiseFloor = MAD(all ratios) * 1.4826\n788:                   stop if latest ratio <= noiseFloor\n789:                c) Question entropy (w=0.35):\n790:                   coverage = answered / total questions\n791:                   stop if coverage >= 0.85\n792:                Redistribute weights for unavailable signals.\n793:                if weighted_stop_score > 0.60: inline_stop_candidate = true\n794:                Combined stop rule: STOP only if the inline 3-signal vote says STOP AND graph_decision is STOP_ALLOWED or absent.\n795:                if inline_stop_candidate and graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\":\n796:                  decision = \"BLOCKED\"\n797:                  reason = \"blockedStop\"\n798:                  stop_blocked = true\n799:                  blocked_by_json = JSON array derived from graph_blockers_json\n800:                  blocked_by_csv = comma-separated blocker names derived from graph_blockers_json\n801:                  gate_convergence_pass = false\n802:                  gate_convergence_score = graph_convergence_score\n803:                  gate_key_question_coverage_pass = no blocker named questionCoverage\n804:                  gate_evidence_density_pass = no blocker named sourceDiversity or evidenceDepth\n805:                  gate_evidence_density_sources = graph_signals_json.sourceDiversity or 0\n806:                  gate_hotspot_saturation_pass = true\n807:                  recovery_strategy = first blocker reason/message, else \"Collect deeper graph evidence before stopping.\"\n808:                else if inline_stop_candidate and (graph_decision == \"STOP_ALLOWED\" or graph_decision is absent):\n809:                  decision = \"STOP\"\n810:                  reason = \"composite_converged\"\n811:                  stop_blocked = false\n812:           6. else: CONTINUE\n813:           7. if decision == \"STOP\" and reason != \"maxIterationsReached\" and effective_min_iterations > 1 and iteration_count < effective_min_iterations:\n814:                decision = \"CONTINUE\"\n815:                reason = \"minIterationsNotReached\"\n816:                min_iterations_guard_blocked = true\n817:                min_iterations_guard_pass = false\n818:           8. if effective_min_iterations > 1 and iteration_count >= effective_min_iterations and min_iterations_guard_already_passed == false:\n819:                min_iterations_guard_pass = true\n820:           9. if decision == \"STOP\" and reason != \"maxIterationsReached\":\n821:                guardResult = checkQualityGuards(state, strategy)\n822:                if not guardResult.passed:\n823:                  log: \"Quality guard failed: {guardResult.violations}. Overriding STOP to CONTINUE.\"\n824:                  decision = \"CONTINUE\"\n825:           See convergence.md for full pseudocode and signal definitions.\n826:           Segment-aware convergence is experimental/reference-only; live workflow uses the current session as a single segment.\n827:         outputs:\n828:           - decision: \"STOP | BLOCKED | STUCK_RECOVERY | CONTINUE\"\n829:           - reason: \"Human-readable stop reason\"\n830:           - stop_blocked: \"Boolean marker set when graph convergence vetoes an inline STOP candidate\"\n831:           - blocked_by_json: \"JSON array of graph blocker names when decision == BLOCKED\"\n832:           - blocked_by_csv: \"Comma-separated graph blocker names when decision == BLOCKED\"\n833:           - gate_convergence_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for the graph-assisted convergence gate\"\n834:           - gate_convergence_score: \"Numeric score recorded from graph convergence\"\n835:           - gate_key_question_coverage_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail derived from graph blocker coverage signals\"\n836:           - gate_evidence_density_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail derived from graph blocker evidence-depth signals\"\n837:           - gate_evidence_density_sources: \"Source-diversity count or equivalent evidence-depth proxy\"\n838:           - gate_hotspot_saturation_pass: \"Research placeholder gate; true unless an explicit blocker sets otherwise\"\n839:           - recovery_strategy: \"One-line hint describing the next research action when decision == BLOCKED or STUCK_RECOVERY\"\n840:           - min_iterations_guard_pass: \"Boolean true when the configured convergence floor has cleared for the first time\"\n841:           - min_iterations_guard_blocked: \"Boolean true when the configured convergence floor overrides a STOP candidate to CONTINUE\"\n842: \n843:       step_emit_min_iterations_guard_pass:\n844:         action: \"Persist a first-class event when the convergence floor clears\"\n845:         if_pass:\n846:           append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"min_iterations_guard_pass\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"iterationCount\":{iteration_count},\"minIterations\":{effective_min_iterations},\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n847:           log: \"Minimum iteration floor cleared for convergence stopping.\"\n848: \n849:       step_emit_blocked_stop:\n850:         action: \"Persist a first-class blocked_stop event when the legal-stop decision tree returns blocked\"\n851:         if_blocked:\n852:           append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"blocked_stop\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"blockedBy\":{blocked_by_json},\"gateResults\":{\"convergence\":{\"pass\":{gate_convergence_pass},\"score\":{gate_convergence_score}},\"keyQuestionCoverage\":{\"pass\":{gate_key_question_coverage_pass},\"answered\":{answered_count},\"total\":{total_questions}},\"evidenceDensity\":{\"pass\":{gate_evidence_density_pass},\"sources\":{gate_evidence_density_sources}},\"hotspotSaturation\":{\"pass\":{gate_hotspot_saturation_pass}}},\"recoveryStrategy\":\"{recovery_strategy}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n853:           log: \"Graph convergence blocked STOP. Failed blockers: {blocked_by_csv}. Recovery strategy: {recovery_strategy}\"\n854:           set:\n855:             decision: \"CONTINUE\"\n856:             reason: \"blockedStop\"\n857:             stop_blocked: false\n858: \n859:       step_handle_convergence:\n860:         action: \"Act on convergence decision\"\n861:         if_stop:\n862:           branch_on: \"convergence_mode == 'divergent' AND reason is in ['composite_converged', 'all_questions_answered']\"\n863:           if_divergent_eligible:\n864:             eligibility_contract:\n865:               required_decision: \"STOP\"\n866:               eligible_reasons: [composite_converged, all_questions_answered]\n867:               excluded_reasons: [maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, minIterationsNotReached, error, manualStop, userPaused]\n868:               fail_closed: \"Any missing or ambiguous reason uses if_existing_terminal_path without preparing a pivot.\"\n869:             steps:\n870:               step_prepare_divergent_pivot:\n871:                 action: \"Generate state-grounded research candidates and prepare or resume the pivot transaction\"\n872:                 command: |\n873:                   node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n874:                   import {\n875:                     buildResearchPivotPreparationInput,\n876:                     renderResearchPivotSeatPrompt,\n877:                   } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/divergent-research-pivot.ts';\n878:                   import {\n879:                     preparePivotTransaction,\n880:                   } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts';\n881: \n882:                   const input = buildResearchPivotPreparationInput({\n883:                     artifactRoot: '{state_paths.packet_dir}',\n884:                     configPath: '{state_paths.config}',\n885:                     stateLogPath: '{state_paths.state_log}',\n886:                     strategyPath: '{state_paths.strategy}',\n887:                     registryPath: '{state_paths.registry}',\n888:                     currentIteration: Number('{current_iteration}'),\n889:                     maxIterations: Number('{max_iterations}'),\n890:                     triggerReason: '{reason}',\n891:                   });\n892:                   const prepared = await preparePivotTransaction(input);\n893:                   const seatPrompts = prepared.status === 'pending'\n894:                     ? Object.fromEntries(prepared.missingSeats.map((seat) => [\n895:                         seat.id,\n896:                         renderResearchPivotSeatPrompt(seat, prepared.dispatchContext),\n897:                       ]))\n898:                     : {};\n899:                   process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify({\n900:                     ...prepared,\n901:                     seatPrompts,\n902:                     boundaryRejections: input.boundaryRejections,\n903:                   })}\\n`);\n904:                   EOF\n905:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n906:                 outputs:\n907:                   - pivot_prepare_json: \"The complete parsed JSON result\"\n908:                   - pivot_prepare_status: \"status from the prepare result\"\n909:                   - pivot_id: \"pivotId from the prepare result\"\n910:                   - pivot_paths_json: \"paths from the prepare result as JSON\"\n911:                   - pivot_resumed: \"resumed from the prepare result\"\n912:                   - pivot_missing_seat_ids: \"missingSeats ids from a pending result\"\n913:                   - pivot_seat_001_json: \"The seat-001 mandate object from missingSeats\"\n914:                   - pivot_seat_002_json: \"The seat-002 mandate object from missingSeats\"\n915:                   - pivot_seat_003_json: \"The seat-003 mandate object from missingSeats\"\n916:                   - pivot_seat_001_prompt: \"seatPrompts['seat-001']\"\n917:                   - pivot_seat_002_prompt: \"seatPrompts['seat-002']\"\n918:                   - pivot_seat_003_prompt: \"seatPrompts['seat-003']\"\n919:                   - pivot_dispatch_context_json: \"dispatchContext from a pending result as JSON\"\n920:                 short_circuit: \"When status is completed or failed, skip all dispatch and record steps and bind this result as pivot_result.\"\n921: \n922:               step_dispatch_pivot_seat_001:\n923:                 action: \"Natively dispatch the analytical research direction-selection seat\"\n924:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain 'seat-001'\"\n925:                 capture_timing: true\n926:                 if_native:\n927:                   dispatch:\n928:                     agent: deep-research\n929:                     model: opus\n930:                     context_source: \"pivot_seat_001_prompt\"\n931:                   wait_for_completion: true\n932:                 failure_contract: \"A native dispatch failure binds status=rejected, a {name,message} error, and the measured timestamps/duration, then proceeds to step_record_pivot_seat_001.\"\n933:                 outputs:\n934:                   - pivot_seat_001_dispatch_status: \"fulfilled or rejected\"\n935:                   - pivot_seat_001_output_json: \"Raw native return serialized as JSON when fulfilled\"\n936:                   - pivot_seat_001_error_json: \"{name,message} when rejected\"\n937:                   - pivot_seat_001_started_at_iso: \"Dispatch start timestamp\"\n938:                   - pivot_seat_001_completed_at_iso: \"Dispatch completion timestamp\"\n939:                   - pivot_seat_001_duration_ms: \"Dispatch duration in milliseconds\"\n940: \n941:               step_record_pivot_seat_001:\n942:                 action: \"Durably record the seat-001 native dispatch outcome\"\n943:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain 'seat-001'\"\n944:                 command: |\n945:                   node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n946:                   import { recordPivotSeatResult } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts';\n947:                   const status = '{pivot_seat_001_dispatch_status}';\n948:                   const outcome = status === 'fulfilled'\n949:                     ? { status, output: {pivot_seat_001_output_json}, startedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_001_started_at_iso}', completedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_001_completed_at_iso}', durationMs: Number('{pivot_seat_001_duration_ms}') }\n950:                     : { status: 'rejected', error: {pivot_seat_001_error_json}, startedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_001_started_at_iso}', completedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_001_completed_at_iso}', durationMs: Number('{pivot_seat_001_duration_ms}') };\n951:                   process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify(recordPivotSeatResult({ paths: {pivot_paths_json}, pivotId: '{pivot_id}', seat: {pivot_seat_001_json}, outcome }))}\\n`);\n952:                   EOF\n953:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n954: \n955:               step_dispatch_pivot_seat_002:\n956:                 action: \"Natively dispatch the critical research direction-selection seat\"\n957:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain 'seat-002'\"\n958:                 capture_timing: true\n959:                 if_native:\n960:                   dispatch:\n961:                     agent: deep-research\n962:                     model: opus\n963:                     context_source: \"pivot_seat_002_prompt\"\n964:                   wait_for_completion: true\n965:                 failure_contract: \"A native dispatch failure binds status=rejected, a {name,message} error, and the measured timestamps/duration, then proceeds to step_record_pivot_seat_002.\"\n966:                 outputs:\n967:                   - pivot_seat_002_dispatch_status: \"fulfilled or rejected\"\n968:                   - pivot_seat_002_output_json: \"Raw native return serialized as JSON when fulfilled\"\n969:                   - pivot_seat_002_error_json: \"{name,message} when rejected\"\n970:                   - pivot_seat_002_started_at_iso: \"Dispatch start timestamp\"\n971:                   - pivot_seat_002_completed_at_iso: \"Dispatch completion timestamp\"\n972:                   - pivot_seat_002_duration_ms: \"Dispatch duration in milliseconds\"\n973: \n974:               step_record_pivot_seat_002:\n975:                 action: \"Durably record the seat-002 native dispatch outcome\"\n976:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain 'seat-002'\"\n977:                 command: |\n978:                   node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n979:                   import { recordPivotSeatResult } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts';\n980:                   const status = '{pivot_seat_002_dispatch_status}';\n981:                   const outcome = status === 'fulfilled'\n982:                     ? { status, output: {pivot_seat_002_output_json}, startedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_002_started_at_iso}', completedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_002_completed_at_iso}', durationMs: Number('{pivot_seat_002_duration_ms}') }\n983:                     : { status: 'rejected', error: {pivot_seat_002_error_json}, startedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_002_started_at_iso}', completedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_002_completed_at_iso}', durationMs: Number('{pivot_seat_002_duration_ms}') };\n984:                   process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify(recordPivotSeatResult({ paths: {pivot_paths_json}, pivotId: '{pivot_id}', seat: {pivot_seat_002_json}, outcome }))}\\n`);\n985:                   EOF\n986:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n987: \n988:               step_dispatch_pivot_seat_003:\n989:                 action: \"Natively dispatch the pragmatic research direction-selection seat\"\n990:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain 'seat-003'\"\n991:                 capture_timing: true\n992:                 if_native:\n993:                   dispatch:\n994:                     agent: deep-research\n995:                     model: opus\n996:                     context_source: \"pivot_seat_003_prompt\"\n997:                   wait_for_completion: true\n998:                 failure_contract: \"A native dispatch failure binds status=rejected, a {name,message} error, and the measured timestamps/duration, then proceeds to step_record_pivot_seat_003.\"\n999:                 outputs:\n1000:                   - pivot_seat_003_dispatch_status: \"fulfilled or rejected\"\n1001:                   - pivot_seat_003_output_json: \"Raw native return serialized as JSON when fulfilled\"\n1002:                   - pivot_seat_003_error_json: \"{name,message} when rejected\"\n1003:                   - pivot_seat_003_started_at_iso: \"Dispatch start timestamp\"\n1004:                   - pivot_seat_003_completed_at_iso: \"Dispatch completion timestamp\"\n1005:                   - pivot_seat_003_duration_ms: \"Dispatch duration in milliseconds\"\n1006: \n1007:               step_record_pivot_seat_003:\n1008:                 action: \"Durably record the seat-003 native dispatch outcome\"\n1009:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain 'seat-003'\"\n1010:                 command: |\n1011:                   node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n1012:                   import { recordPivotSeatResult } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts';\n1013:                   const status = '{pivot_seat_003_dispatch_status}';\n1014:                   const outcome = status === 'fulfilled'\n1015:                     ? { status, output: {pivot_seat_003_output_json}, startedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_003_started_at_iso}', completedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_003_completed_at_iso}', durationMs: Number('{pivot_seat_003_duration_ms}') }\n1016:                     : { status: 'rejected', error: {pivot_seat_003_error_json}, startedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_003_started_at_iso}', completedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_003_completed_at_iso}', durationMs: Number('{pivot_seat_003_duration_ms}') };\n1017:                   process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify(recordPivotSeatResult({ paths: {pivot_paths_json}, pivotId: '{pivot_id}', seat: {pivot_seat_003_json}, outcome }))}\\n`);\n1018:                   EOF\n1019:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1020: \n1021:               step_finalize_divergent_pivot:\n1022:                 action: \"Finalize the prepared pivot after all missing native seats are durable\"\n1023:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending'\"\n1024:                 command: |\n1025:                   node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n1026:                   import { finalizePivotTransaction } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts';\n1027:                   process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify(finalizePivotTransaction({ paths: {pivot_paths_json}, pivotId: '{pivot_id}', resumed: {pivot_resumed} }))}\\n`);\n1028:                   EOF\n1029:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1030:                 outputs:\n1031:                   - pivot_finalize_json: \"The complete parsed final result\"\n1032: \n1033:               step_resolve_divergent_pivot_result:\n1034:                 action: \"Use prepare's terminal result on resume/short-circuit, otherwise use finalize's result\"\n1035:                 branch_on: \"pivot_prepare_status\"\n1036:                 if_pending: { bind: { pivot_result: \"{pivot_finalize_json}\" } }\n1037:                 if_completed_or_failed: { bind: { pivot_result: \"{pivot_prepare_json}\" } }\n1038: \n1039:               step_apply_divergent_pivot_result:\n1040:                 action: \"Adopt a successful focus or fail closed to the existing synthesis path\"\n1041:                 branch_on: \"pivot_result.status\"\n1042:                 if_completed:\n1043:                   set:\n1044:                     next_focus: \"{pivot_result.restoredFocus}\"\n1045:                     pivot_lineage: \"Pivot {pivot_result.pivotId} selected {pivot_result.selectedCandidate.id} from source iteration {current_iteration}.\"\n1046:                     saturated_directions: \"{pivot_result.completedEvent.saturatedDirections}\"\n1047:                   command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg}\"\n1048:                   log: \"Divergent pivot {pivot_result.pivotId} restored focus to {pivot_result.restoredFocus}; continuing iteration {current_iteration}.\"\n1049:                   proceed_to: step_rejected_pattern_cache\n1050:                 if_failed:\n1051:                   log: \"Divergent pivot {pivot_result.pivotId} failed closed ({pivot_result.failureReason}); proceeding to synthesis.\"\n1052:                   skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1053:             on_error:\n1054:               log: \"Divergent pivot integration error; failing closed to the existing synthesis path.\"\n1055:               skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1056:           if_existing_terminal_path:\n1057:             log: \"Loop stopping. Reason: {reason}\"\n1058:             skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1059:         if_stuck_recovery:\n1060:           append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"stuckRecovery\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"stopReason\":\"stuckRecovery\",\"fromIteration\":{current_iteration},\"outcome\":\"recovered\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n1061:           log: \"Stuck detected ({stuck_count} consecutive no-progress). Entering recovery.\"\n1062:           set: { next_focus: \"RECOVERY: Widen scope. Try fundamentally different approach. Least-explored question: {least_explored}\" }\n1063:           reset: { stuck_count: 0 }\n1064:         if_continue:\n1065:           log: \"Iteration {current_iteration}: Continuing. Focus: {next_focus}\"\n1066: \n1067:       step_rejected_pattern_cache:\n1068:         action: \"Apply reducer-derived rejected-pattern suppression before dispatch candidate selection\"\n1069:         read:\n1070:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1071:           - \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n1072:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1073:         candidate_sources:\n1074:           next_focus:\n1075:             category: \"next-focus\"\n1076:             values:\n1077:               - \"{next_focus}\"\n1078:               - \"{remaining_questions_list}\"\n1079:               - \"{carried_forward_open_questions}\"\n1080:           recovery:\n1081:             category: \"recovery\"\n1082:             values:\n1083:               - \"{recovery_strategy}\"\n1084:               - \"{least_explored}\"\n1085:           ideas:\n1086:             category: \"ideas\"\n1087:             values:\n1088:               - \"{promoted_ideas_list}\"\n1089:             optional_file: \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/research-ideas.md\"\n1090:         algorithm: |\n1091:           Use registry.rejectedPatternIndex and registry.promotedIdeas from the latest\n1092:           reducer pass as the source of truth.\n1093:           Compare normalized exact text first. Then compare fuzzy similarity with\n1094:           rejected_pattern_fuzzy_threshold, but only when candidate and rejected categories\n1095:           are compatible. Remove suppressed candidates from next_focus, recovery, and ideas\n1096:           selection before rendering the dispatch prompt. If all candidates are suppressed,\n1097:           halt for operator input instead of reusing a rejected idea.\n1098:         outputs:\n1099:           - accepted_next_focus: \"First unsuppressed next-focus candidate, or null\"\n1100:           - accepted_recovery_candidate: \"First unsuppressed recovery candidate, or null\"\n1101:           - accepted_idea_candidate: \"First unsuppressed ideas candidate, or null\"\n1102:           - rejected_candidate_matches: \"Suppressed candidate diagnostics from registry.suppressedCandidates plus any current-step matches\"\n1103:         if_next_focus_suppressed:\n1104:           set: { next_focus: \"{accepted_next_focus || accepted_recovery_candidate || accepted_idea_candidate}\" }\n1105:           log: \"Rejected-pattern cache suppressed the prior candidate; dispatching the next accepted candidate.\"\n1106:         if_all_candidates_suppressed:\n1107:           halt: true\n1108:           message: 'All next-focus, recovery, and ideas candidates match active rejected patterns. Remove or reset the rejected pattern, or provide a new focus. In a ledger-backed run (a deep-research-ledger/frames folder beside the state log) the next projection replaces a hand-edited state log, so record the removal or reset through the append gateway: write one row to a file, either {\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"idea_rejected_removed\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"pattern\":\"<rejected text>\",\"category\":\"<its category>\",\"timestamp\":\"<UTC now, e.g. 2026-05-24T00:00:00Z>\"} or {\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"idea_rejected_reset\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"reason\":\"<why>\",\"timestamp\":\"<UTC now>\"}, then run node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode research --run-directory {artifact_dir} --event-json <that file> and rerun the reducer before resuming.'\n1109: \n1110:       step_ideas_backlog_lifecycle:\n1111:         action: \"Track reducer-owned observed/promoted/rejected idea lifecycle before dispatch\"\n1112:         read:\n1113:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1114:           - \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n1115:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1116:         lifecycle:\n1117:           observed_event: \"idea_observed\"\n1118:           promoted_event: \"idea_promoted\"\n1119:           rejected_event: \"idea_rejected\"\n1120:           min_observations: \"{min_idea_observations}\"\n1121:           authority: \"Leaf agents emit observations only; reducer emits promotions and owns ranking.\"\n1122:         validate:\n1123:           - \"If new leaf-authored output includes idea_promoted, fail validation; only reducer output may append idea_promoted.\"\n1124:           - \"If promoted_ideas_count > 0 and next_focus is empty or all questions are resolved, prefer the first unsuppressed promoted idea.\"\n1125:           - \"If suppressed_ideas_count > 0, do not render those ideas into dispatch context.\"\n1126:         outputs:\n1127:           - observed_ideas_count: \"Reducer-derived observed ideas count\"\n1128:           - promoted_ideas_count: \"Reducer-derived promoted ideas count after minIdeaObservations\"\n1129:           - suppressed_ideas_count: \"Reducer-derived rejected/suppressed ideas count\"\n1130:           - accepted_idea_candidate: \"First unsuppressed promoted idea, or null\"\n1131: \n1132:       step_normalize_pause_events:\n1133:         action: \"Normalize pause and recovery lifecycle events to the frozen STOP_REASONS enum at emission time\"\n1134:         stop_reasons_enum: [converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused]\n1135:         rule_pause_sentinel:\n1136:           raw_event_forbidden: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"paused\"}'\n1137:           canonical_event: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"userPaused\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"stopReason\":\"userPaused\",\"sentinelPath\":\"{state_paths.pause_sentinel}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n1138:         rule_stuck_recovery:\n1139:           raw_event_forbidden: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"stuck_recovery\"}'\n1140:           canonical_event: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"stuckRecovery\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"stopReason\":\"stuckRecovery\",\"fromIteration\":{current_iteration},\"outcome\":\"recovered\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n1141: \n1142:       step_marker_scan:\n1143:         action: \"H-2 loop-prevention guard: scan previous iteration's rendered prompt for nested research marker\"\n1144:         canonical_header: \"DEEP-RESEARCH\"\n1145:         nested_marker_pattern: \"^(DEEP-REVIEW|CODE-REVIEW)$\"\n1146:         algorithm: |\n1147:           if current_iteration > 1:\n1148:             PREV_PROMPT_PATH = \"{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{previous_iteration}.md\"\n1149:             if file_exists(PREV_PROMPT_PATH):\n1150:               PREV_PROMPT_FIRST_LINE = head -1 of PREV_PROMPT_PATH\n1151:               if PREV_PROMPT_FIRST_LINE matches nested_marker_pattern:\n1152:                 log \"ERROR: nested research-of-review loop detected (review marker found in previous iteration prompt). Aborting.\"\n1153:                 halt with exit code 2\n1154:         note: |\n1155:           False-positive prevention: a research prompt that starts with its own canonical\n1156:           header is this loop's own iteration output, never a nested dispatch; only a review\n1157:           marker is, so the guard matches nested_marker_pattern rather than the canonical\n1158:           header. Markers appearing in comments or body text are ignored. True-positive\n1159:           triggers only when a previous iteration's rendered prompt literally starts with a\n1160:           review marker, indicating a nested research-of-review dispatch.\n1161: \n1162:       step_dispatch_iteration:\n1163:         action: \"Dispatch one iteration via the selected executor\"\n1164:         resolve_executor:\n1165:           source: \"config.executor\"\n1166:           loader: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts#parseExecutorConfig\"\n1167:         pre_dispatch:\n1168:           generate_summary: |\n1169:             STATE SUMMARY (auto-generated):\n1170:             Segment: {current_segment} | Iteration: {current_iteration} of {max_iterations}\n1171:             Questions: {answered_count}/{total_questions} answered | Last focus: {last_focus}\n1172:             Last 2 ratios: {ratio_prev} -> {ratio_latest} | Stuck count: {stuck_count}\n1173:             {resource_map_prompt_line}\n1174:             {lineage_context_prompt_line}\n1175:             Next focus: {next_focus}\n1176:           render_prompt_pack:\n1177:             template_path: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl\"\n1178:             renderer: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/prompt-pack.ts#renderPromptPack\"\n1179:             output_path: \"{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md\"\n1180:             variables:\n1181:               state_summary: \"{state_summary}\"\n1182:               research_topic: \"{research_topic}\"\n1183:               current_iteration: \"{current_iteration}\"\n1184:               max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n1185:               next_focus: \"{next_focus}\"\n1186:               remaining_questions_list: \"{remaining_questions_list}\"\n1187:               carried_forward_open_questions: \"{carried_forward_open_questions}\"\n1188:               last_3_summaries: \"{last_3_summaries}\"\n1189:               pivot_lineage: \"{pivot_lineage}\"\n1190:               saturated_directions: \"{saturated_directions}\"\n1191:               state_paths_config: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1192:               state_paths_state_log: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1193:               state_paths_strategy: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1194:               state_paths_registry: \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n1195:               state_paths_iteration_pattern: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1196:               state_paths_delta_pattern: \"{state_paths.delta_pattern}\"\n1197:         pre_dispatch_audit:\n1198:           skip_when: \"config.executor.type == 'native'\"\n1199:           call: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts#writeFirstRecordExecutor\"\n1200:           args:\n1201:             stateLogPath: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1202:             executor: \"{config.executor}\"\n1203:             iteration: \"{current_iteration}\"\n1204:         branch_on: \"config.executor.type\"\n1205:         if_native:\n1206:           dispatch:\n1207:             agent: deep-research\n1208:             model: opus\n1209:             context_source: \"rendered_prompt_pack\"\n1210:           wait_for_completion: true\n1211:         if_cli_claude_code:\n1212:           command: |\n1213:             node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n1214:             import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n1215:             import { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\n1216: \n1217:             import { runAuditedExecutorCommand } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts';\n1218:             import { resolveClaudePermissionMode } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts';\n1219: \n1220:             const executor = {\n1221:               kind: 'cli-claude-code',\n1222:               model: '{config.executor.model}',\n1223:               reasoningEffort: '{config.executor.reasoningEffort}' === 'null' ? null : '{config.executor.reasoningEffort}',\n1224:               serviceTier: '{config.executor.serviceTier}' === 'null' ? null : '{config.executor.serviceTier}',\n1225:               sandboxMode: '{config.executor.sandboxMode}' === 'null' ? null : '{config.executor.sandboxMode}',\n1226:               timeoutSeconds: Number('{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}'),\n1227:             };\n1228:             const args = [\n1229:               '-p',\n1230:               readFileSync('{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md', 'utf8'),\n1231:               '--model',\n1232:               executor.model,\n1233:               '--permission-mode',\n1234:               resolveClaudePermissionMode(executor.sandboxMode),\n1235:               '--output-format',\n1236:               'text',\n1237:             ];\n1238:             if (executor.reasoningEffort) {\n1239:               args.push('--effort', executor.reasoningEffort);\n1240:             }\n1241: \n1242:             const dispatchFacts = {\n1243:               command: 'deep/research',\n1244:               mode: 'research',\n1245:               specFolder: '{spec_folder}',\n1246:               artifactDir: '{state_paths.packet_dir}',\n1247:               iteration: Number('{current_iteration}'),\n1248:               executorKind: '{config.executor.type}',\n1249:               branchId: '{config.executor.type}',\n1250:               sessionId: '{config.lineage.sessionId}',\n1251:               generation: Number('{config.lineage.generation}'),\n1252:             };\n1253:             const dispatchId = 'research-i{current_iteration}-g{config.lineage.generation}';\n1254:             process.exit(\n1255:               runAuditedExecutorCommand({\n1256:                 command: 'claude',\n1257:                 args,\n1258:                 cwd: '{repo_root}',\n1259:                 timeoutSeconds: executor.timeoutSeconds,\n1260:                 stateLogPath: '{state_paths.state_log}',\n1261:                 executor,\n1262:                 iteration: Number('{current_iteration}'),\n1263:                 receiptDir: '{state_paths.packet_dir}/dispatch-receipts',\n1264:                 dispatchId,\n1265:               }),\n1266:             );\n1267:             EOF\n1268:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1269:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1270:           wait_for_completion: true\n1271:           notes:\n1272:             - \"sandboxMode maps to permission-mode: read-only -> plan, workspace-write -> acceptEdits, danger-full-access -> bypassPermissions\"\n1273:             - \"claude-code has no serviceTier flag\"\n1274:             - \"claude-code supports --effort for reasoning depth\"\n1275:         if_cli_cursor:\n1276:           command: |\n1277:             node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n1278:             import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n1279:             import { createRequire } from 'node:module';\n1280:             import { runAuditedExecutorCommand } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts';\n1281:             import { resolveSandboxMode, resolveClaudePermissionMode } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts';\n1282:             import {\n1283:               snapshotOutOfScopeDirtyPaths,\n1284:               enforceWriteContainment,\n1285:             } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/write-containment.ts';\n1286: \n1287:             // cursor-agent/devin/pi have no single-executor branch of their own, so\n1288:             // without this they silently degrade to native. The command builder is the\n1289:             // same one the fan-out lineage path uses, so the enforced model allowlist,\n1290:             // headless write-mode flags, and binary preflight stay one source of truth.\n1291:             // It throws (fail closed) when the binary is absent or the model is off the\n1292:             // allowlist, so a requested CLI executor never becomes native.\n1293:             const require = createRequire(import.meta.url);\n1294:             const { buildLineageCommand } = require('./.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs');\n1295: \n1296:             const kind = '{config.executor.type}';\n1297:             const model = '{config.executor.model}' === 'null' ? null : '{config.executor.model}';\n1298:             const timeoutSeconds = Number('{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}');\n1299:             // The iteration must write its own iteration file, delta and state record,\n1300:             // so the leaf runs workspace-write; the builder maps that to each CLI's real\n1301:             // write-permitting headless flags.\n1302:             const sandboxMode = 'workspace-write';\n1303:             const lineage = { kind, model, sandboxMode };\n1304:             const resolvedSandbox = resolveSandboxMode(sandboxMode);\n1305:             const resolvedPermission = resolveClaudePermissionMode(sandboxMode);\n1306: \n1307:             const repoRoot = '{repo_root}';\n1308:             const promptBody = readFileSync('{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md', 'utf8');\n1309:             const { command, args, input } = buildLineageCommand(\n1310:               lineage,\n1311:               promptBody,\n1312:               resolvedSandbox,\n1313:               resolvedPermission,\n1314:               { env: process.env, cwd: repoRoot },\n1315:             );\n1316: \n1317:             const executor = {\n1318:               kind,\n1319:               model,\n1320:               configDir: null,\n1321:               reasoningEffort: null,\n1322:               serviceTier: null,\n1323:               sandboxMode,\n1324:               timeoutSeconds,\n1325:               governor: null,\n1326:             };\n1327:             const dispatchId = 'research-i{current_iteration}-g{generation}';\n1328:             const artifactDir = '{artifact_dir}';\n1329:             const preDispatchDirtyPaths = snapshotOutOfScopeDirtyPaths({ repoRoot, artifactDir });\n1330:             const dispatchExit = runAuditedExecutorCommand({\n1331:               command,\n1332:               args,\n1333:               cwd: repoRoot,\n1334:               timeoutSeconds,\n1335:               stateLogPath: '{state_paths.state_log}',\n1336:               executor,\n1337:               iteration: Number('{current_iteration}'),\n1338:               input,\n1339:               receiptDir: '{state_paths.packet_dir}/dispatch-receipts',\n1340:               dispatchId,\n1341:             });\n1342:             const containment = enforceWriteContainment({\n1343:               repoRoot,\n1344:               artifactDir,\n1345:               preDispatchDirtyPaths,\n1346:               stateLogPath: '{state_paths.state_log}',\n1347:               iteration: Number('{current_iteration}'),\n1348:               label: dispatchId,\n1349:             });\n1350:             if (containment.violations.length > 0) {\n1351:               console.error(\n1352:                 'write-containment advisory: detected ' + containment.violations.length\n1353:                   + ' out-of-scope path(s), left on disk: '\n1354:                   + containment.violations.map((v) => v.path).join(', '),\n1355:               );\n1356:             }\n1357:             process.exit(dispatchExit);\n1358:             EOF\n1359:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1360:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1361:           wait_for_completion: true\n1362:           notes:\n1363:             - \"cli-cursor single-executor: dispatches per-iteration through the shared fan-out command builder (buildLineageCommand) so the enforced cli-cursor model allowlist + headless write flags stay one source of truth; runAuditedExecutorCommand emits INTENT + COMPLETION receipts\"\n1364:             - \"Fails closed when cursor-agent is absent or the model is off the allowlist (buildLineageCommand throws, exit non-zero) — a requested cli-cursor executor never degrades to native\"\n1365:         if_cli_devin:\n1366:           command: |\n1367:             node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n1368:             import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n1369:             import { createRequire } from 'node:module';\n1370:             import { runAuditedExecutorCommand } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts';\n1371:             import { resolveSandboxMode, resolveClaudePermissionMode } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts';\n1372:             import {\n1373:               snapshotOutOfScopeDirtyPaths,\n1374:               enforceWriteContainment,\n1375:             } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/write-containment.ts';\n1376: \n1377:             // cursor-agent/devin/pi have no single-executor branch of their own, so\n1378:             // without this they silently degrade to native. The command builder is the\n1379:             // same one the fan-out lineage path uses, so the enforced model allowlist,\n1380:             // headless write-mode flags, and binary preflight stay one source of truth.\n1381:             // It throws (fail closed) when the binary is absent or the model is off the\n1382:             // allowlist, so a requested CLI executor never becomes native.\n1383:             const require = createRequire(import.meta.url);\n1384:             const { buildLineageCommand } = require('./.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs');\n1385: \n1386:             const kind = '{config.executor.type}';\n1387:             const model = '{config.executor.model}' === 'null' ? null : '{config.executor.model}';\n1388:             const timeoutSeconds = Number('{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}');\n1389:             // The iteration must write its own iteration file, delta and state record,\n1390:             // so the leaf runs workspace-write; the builder maps that to each CLI's real\n1391:             // write-permitting headless flags.\n1392:             const sandboxMode = 'workspace-write';\n1393:             const lineage = { kind, model, sandboxMode };\n1394:             const resolvedSandbox = resolveSandboxMode(sandboxMode);\n1395:             const resolvedPermission = resolveClaudePermissionMode(sandboxMode);\n1396: \n1397:             const repoRoot = '{repo_root}';\n1398:             const promptBody = readFileSync('{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md', 'utf8');\n1399:             const { command, args, input } = buildLineageCommand(\n1400:               lineage,\n1401:               promptBody,\n1402:               resolvedSandbox,\n1403:               resolvedPermission,\n1404:               { env: process.env, cwd: repoRoot },\n1405:             );\n1406: \n1407:             const executor = {\n1408:               kind,\n1409:               model,\n1410:               configDir: null,\n1411:               reasoningEffort: null,\n1412:               serviceTier: null,\n1413:               sandboxMode,\n1414:               timeoutSeconds,\n1415:               governor: null,\n1416:             };\n1417:             const dispatchId = 'research-i{current_iteration}-g{generation}';\n1418:             const artifactDir = '{artifact_dir}';\n1419:             const preDispatchDirtyPaths = snapshotOutOfScopeDirtyPaths({ repoRoot, artifactDir });\n1420:             const dispatchExit = runAuditedExecutorCommand({\n1421:               command,\n1422:               args,\n1423:               cwd: repoRoot,\n1424:               timeoutSeconds,\n1425:               stateLogPath: '{state_paths.state_log}',\n1426:               executor,\n1427:               iteration: Number('{current_iteration}'),\n1428:               input,\n1429:               receiptDir: '{state_paths.packet_dir}/dispatch-receipts',\n1430:               dispatchId,\n1431:             });\n1432:             const containment = enforceWriteContainment({\n1433:               repoRoot,\n1434:               artifactDir,\n1435:               preDispatchDirtyPaths,\n1436:               stateLogPath: '{state_paths.state_log}',\n1437:               iteration: Number('{current_iteration}'),\n1438:               label: dispatchId,\n1439:             });\n1440:             if (containment.violations.length > 0) {\n1441:               console.error(\n1442:                 'write-containment advisory: detected ' + containment.violations.length\n1443:                   + ' out-of-scope path(s), left on disk: '\n1444:                   + containment.violations.map((v) => v.path).join(', '),\n1445:               );\n1446:             }\n1447:             process.exit(dispatchExit);\n1448:             EOF\n1449:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1450:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 1451]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml, lines 751-1450\n751:           bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"config_warning\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"field\":\"minIterations\",\"configured\":{min_iterations_raw},\"effective\":{effective_min_iterations},\"maxIterations\":{max_iterations},\"message\":\"minIterations exceeds maxIterations; clamping to the hard cap.\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n752:           log: \"minIterations exceeds maxIterations; clamping to the hard cap.\"\n753:         if_convergence_mode_invalid:\n754:           bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"config_warning\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"field\":\"convergenceMode\",\"fallback\":\"default\",\"message\":\"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n755:           log: \"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\"\n756: \n757:       step_graph_convergence:\n758:         action: \"Evaluate coverage-graph convergence before the inline 3-signal vote and persist the graph decision snapshot\"\n759:         bash: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"research\" --session-id \"{config.lineage.sessionId}\" --convergence-mode \"{convergence_mode}\" --persist-snapshot --iteration \"{current_iteration}\"'\n760:         note: \"Run before the inline vote. STOP from the inline 3-signal vote is allowed only when the graph decision is STOP_ALLOWED or absent.\"\n761:         outputs:\n762:           - graph_decision: \"Tool decision value (CONTINUE | STOP_ALLOWED | STOP_BLOCKED), else null when unavailable\"\n763:           - graph_decision_json: \"JSON-encoded graph decision string, else null\"\n764:           - graph_signals_json: \"Tool signals object, else {}\"\n765:           - graph_blockers_json: \"Tool blockers array, else []\"\n766:           - graph_trace_json: \"Tool trace payload, else []\"\n767:           - graph_convergence_score: \"signals.blendedScore when present, else the best available graph score, else 0\"\n768:         bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"graph_convergence\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"decision\":{graph_decision_json},\"signals\":{graph_signals_json},\"blockers\":{graph_blockers_json},\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n769: \n770:       step_check_convergence:\n771:         action: \"Evaluate stop conditions and combine the inline 3-signal vote with graph convergence\"\n772:         algorithm: |\n773:           1. if iteration_count >= max_iterations: STOP (maxIterationsReached). This terminal cap bypasses quality-guard overrides; record failed guards/blockers as synthesis evidence instead of continuing.\n774:           2. if stuck_count >= config.stuckThreshold: STUCK_RECOVERY\n775:           3. if convergence_mode == \"off\": skip convergence stop candidates and continue unless a terminal cap, pause sentinel, or recovery halt has already fired.\n776:           3a. if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: steps 4 and 5 are telemetry only and cannot set STOP or BLOCKED. Record weighted_stop_score for diagnostics, keep decision = \"CONTINUE\" and choose a broader next focus.\n777:           4. if remaining_questions == 0: STOP (all_questions_answered)\n778:           5. GRAPH-ASSISTED COMPOSITE CONVERGENCE:\n779:                step_graph_convergence already recorded graph_decision, graph_signals_json, graph_blockers_json, and graph_convergence_score for this run.\n780:                The existing inline 3-signal vote still computes the inline STOP candidate and is not replaced.\n781:                signals = []\n782:                Filter: exclude iterations where status == thought from signal inputs (use only evidence iterations)\n783:                a) Rolling average (w=0.30, needs 3+ iterations):\n784:                   avg = mean(last 3 newInfoRatios)\n785:                   stop if avg < convergence_threshold\n786:                b) MAD noise floor (w=0.35, needs 4+ iterations):\n787:                   noiseFloor = MAD(all ratios) * 1.4826\n788:                   stop if latest ratio <= noiseFloor\n789:                c) Question entropy (w=0.35):\n790:                   coverage = answered / total questions\n791:                   stop if coverage >= 0.85\n792:                Redistribute weights for unavailable signals.\n793:                if weighted_stop_score > 0.60: inline_stop_candidate = true\n794:                Combined stop rule: STOP only if the inline 3-signal vote says STOP AND graph_decision is STOP_ALLOWED or absent.\n795:                if inline_stop_candidate and graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\":\n796:                  decision = \"BLOCKED\"\n797:                  reason = \"blockedStop\"\n798:                  stop_blocked = true\n799:                  blocked_by_json = JSON array derived from graph_blockers_json\n800:                  blocked_by_csv = comma-separated blocker names derived from graph_blockers_json\n801:                  gate_convergence_pass = false\n802:                  gate_convergence_score = graph_convergence_score\n803:                  gate_key_question_coverage_pass = no blocker named questionCoverage\n804:                  gate_evidence_density_pass = no blocker named sourceDiversity or evidenceDepth\n805:                  gate_evidence_density_sources = graph_signals_json.sourceDiversity or 0\n806:                  gate_hotspot_saturation_pass = true\n807:                  recovery_strategy = first blocker reason/message, else \"Collect deeper graph evidence before stopping.\"\n808:                else if inline_stop_candidate and (graph_decision == \"STOP_ALLOWED\" or graph_decision is absent):\n809:                  decision = \"STOP\"\n810:                  reason = \"composite_converged\"\n811:                  stop_blocked = false\n812:           6. else: CONTINUE\n813:           7. if decision == \"STOP\" and reason != \"maxIterationsReached\" and effective_min_iterations > 1 and iteration_count < effective_min_iterations:\n814:                decision = \"CONTINUE\"\n815:                reason = \"minIterationsNotReached\"\n816:                min_iterations_guard_blocked = true\n817:                min_iterations_guard_pass = false\n818:           8. if effective_min_iterations > 1 and iteration_count >= effective_min_iterations and min_iterations_guard_already_passed == false:\n819:                min_iterations_guard_pass = true\n820:           9. if decision == \"STOP\" and reason != \"maxIterationsReached\":\n821:                guardResult = checkQualityGuards(state, strategy)\n822:                if not guardResult.passed:\n823:                  log: \"Quality guard failed: {guardResult.violations}. Overriding STOP to CONTINUE.\"\n824:                  decision = \"CONTINUE\"\n825:           See convergence.md for full pseudocode and signal definitions.\n826:           Segment-aware convergence is experimental/reference-only; live workflow uses the current session as a single segment.\n827:         outputs:\n828:           - decision: \"STOP | BLOCKED | STUCK_RECOVERY | CONTINUE\"\n829:           - reason: \"Human-readable stop reason\"\n830:           - stop_blocked: \"Boolean marker set when graph convergence vetoes an inline STOP candidate\"\n831:           - blocked_by_json: \"JSON array of graph blocker names when decision == BLOCKED\"\n832:           - blocked_by_csv: \"Comma-separated graph blocker names when decision == BLOCKED\"\n833:           - gate_convergence_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for the graph-assisted convergence gate\"\n834:           - gate_convergence_score: \"Numeric score recorded from graph convergence\"\n835:           - gate_key_question_coverage_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail derived from graph blocker coverage signals\"\n836:           - gate_evidence_density_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail derived from graph blocker evidence-depth signals\"\n837:           - gate_evidence_density_sources: \"Source-diversity count or equivalent evidence-depth proxy\"\n838:           - gate_hotspot_saturation_pass: \"Research placeholder gate; true unless an explicit blocker sets otherwise\"\n839:           - recovery_strategy: \"One-line hint describing the next research action when decision == BLOCKED or STUCK_RECOVERY\"\n840:           - min_iterations_guard_pass: \"Boolean true when the configured convergence floor has cleared for the first time\"\n841:           - min_iterations_guard_blocked: \"Boolean true when the configured convergence floor overrides a STOP candidate to CONTINUE\"\n842: \n843:       step_emit_min_iterations_guard_pass:\n844:         action: \"Persist a first-class event when the convergence floor clears\"\n845:         if_pass:\n846:           append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"min_iterations_guard_pass\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"iterationCount\":{iteration_count},\"minIterations\":{effective_min_iterations},\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n847:           log: \"Minimum iteration floor cleared for convergence stopping.\"\n848: \n849:       step_emit_blocked_stop:\n850:         action: \"Persist a first-class blocked_stop event when the legal-stop decision tree returns blocked\"\n851:         if_blocked:\n852:           append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"blocked_stop\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"blockedBy\":{blocked_by_json},\"gateResults\":{\"convergence\":{\"pass\":{gate_convergence_pass},\"score\":{gate_convergence_score}},\"keyQuestionCoverage\":{\"pass\":{gate_key_question_coverage_pass},\"answered\":{answered_count},\"total\":{total_questions}},\"evidenceDensity\":{\"pass\":{gate_evidence_density_pass},\"sources\":{gate_evidence_density_sources}},\"hotspotSaturation\":{\"pass\":{gate_hotspot_saturation_pass}}},\"recoveryStrategy\":\"{recovery_strategy}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n853:           log: \"Graph convergence blocked STOP. Failed blockers: {blocked_by_csv}. Recovery strategy: {recovery_strategy}\"\n854:           set:\n855:             decision: \"CONTINUE\"\n856:             reason: \"blockedStop\"\n857:             stop_blocked: false\n858: \n859:       step_handle_convergence:\n860:         action: \"Act on convergence decision\"\n861:         if_stop:\n862:           branch_on: \"convergence_mode == 'divergent' AND reason is in ['composite_converged', 'all_questions_answered']\"\n863:           if_divergent_eligible:\n864:             eligibility_contract:\n865:               required_decision: \"STOP\"\n866:               eligible_reasons: [composite_converged, all_questions_answered]\n867:               excluded_reasons: [maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, minIterationsNotReached, error, manualStop, userPaused]\n868:               fail_closed: \"Any missing or ambiguous reason uses if_existing_terminal_path without preparing a pivot.\"\n869:             steps:\n870:               step_prepare_divergent_pivot:\n871:                 action: \"Generate state-grounded research candidates and prepare or resume the pivot transaction\"\n872:                 command: |\n873:                   node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n874:                   import {\n875:                     buildResearchPivotPreparationInput,\n876:                     renderResearchPivotSeatPrompt,\n877:                   } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/divergent-research-pivot.ts';\n878:                   import {\n879:                     preparePivotTransaction,\n880:                   } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts';\n881: \n882:                   const input = buildResearchPivotPreparationInput({\n883:                     artifactRoot: '{state_paths.packet_dir}',\n884:                     configPath: '{state_paths.config}',\n885:                     stateLogPath: '{state_paths.state_log}',\n886:                     strategyPath: '{state_paths.strategy}',\n887:                     registryPath: '{state_paths.registry}',\n888:                     currentIteration: Number('{current_iteration}'),\n889:                     maxIterations: Number('{max_iterations}'),\n890:                     triggerReason: '{reason}',\n891:                   });\n892:                   const prepared = await preparePivotTransaction(input);\n893:                   const seatPrompts = prepared.status === 'pending'\n894:                     ? Object.fromEntries(prepared.missingSeats.map((seat) => [\n895:                         seat.id,\n896:                         renderResearchPivotSeatPrompt(seat, prepared.dispatchContext),\n897:                       ]))\n898:                     : {};\n899:                   process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify({\n900:                     ...prepared,\n901:                     seatPrompts,\n902:                     boundaryRejections: input.boundaryRejections,\n903:                   })}\\n`);\n904:                   EOF\n905:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n906:                 outputs:\n907:                   - pivot_prepare_json: \"The complete parsed JSON result\"\n908:                   - pivot_prepare_status: \"status from the prepare result\"\n909:                   - pivot_id: \"pivotId from the prepare result\"\n910:                   - pivot_paths_json: \"paths from the prepare result as JSON\"\n911:                   - pivot_resumed: \"resumed from the prepare result\"\n912:                   - pivot_missing_seat_ids: \"missingSeats ids from a pending result\"\n913:                   - pivot_seat_001_json: \"The seat-001 mandate object from missingSeats\"\n914:                   - pivot_seat_002_json: \"The seat-002 mandate object from missingSeats\"\n915:                   - pivot_seat_003_json: \"The seat-003 mandate object from missingSeats\"\n916:                   - pivot_seat_001_prompt: \"seatPrompts['seat-001']\"\n917:                   - pivot_seat_002_prompt: \"seatPrompts['seat-002']\"\n918:                   - pivot_seat_003_prompt: \"seatPrompts['seat-003']\"\n919:                   - pivot_dispatch_context_json: \"dispatchContext from a pending result as JSON\"\n920:                 short_circuit: \"When status is completed or failed, skip all dispatch and record steps and bind this result as pivot_result.\"\n921: \n922:               step_dispatch_pivot_seat_001:\n923:                 action: \"Natively dispatch the analytical research direction-selection seat\"\n924:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain 'seat-001'\"\n925:                 capture_timing: true\n926:                 if_native:\n927:                   dispatch:\n928:                     agent: deep-research\n929:                     model: opus\n930:                     context_source: \"pivot_seat_001_prompt\"\n931:                   wait_for_completion: true\n932:                 failure_contract: \"A native dispatch failure binds status=rejected, a {name,message} error, and the measured timestamps/duration, then proceeds to step_record_pivot_seat_001.\"\n933:                 outputs:\n934:                   - pivot_seat_001_dispatch_status: \"fulfilled or rejected\"\n935:                   - pivot_seat_001_output_json: \"Raw native return serialized as JSON when fulfilled\"\n936:                   - pivot_seat_001_error_json: \"{name,message} when rejected\"\n937:                   - pivot_seat_001_started_at_iso: \"Dispatch start timestamp\"\n938:                   - pivot_seat_001_completed_at_iso: \"Dispatch completion timestamp\"\n939:                   - pivot_seat_001_duration_ms: \"Dispatch duration in milliseconds\"\n940: \n941:               step_record_pivot_seat_001:\n942:                 action: \"Durably record the seat-001 native dispatch outcome\"\n943:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain 'seat-001'\"\n944:                 command: |\n945:                   node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n946:                   import { recordPivotSeatResult } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts';\n947:                   const status = '{pivot_seat_001_dispatch_status}';\n948:                   const outcome = status === 'fulfilled'\n949:                     ? { status, output: {pivot_seat_001_output_json}, startedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_001_started_at_iso}', completedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_001_completed_at_iso}', durationMs: Number('{pivot_seat_001_duration_ms}') }\n950:                     : { status: 'rejected', error: {pivot_seat_001_error_json}, startedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_001_started_at_iso}', completedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_001_completed_at_iso}', durationMs: Number('{pivot_seat_001_duration_ms}') };\n951:                   process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify(recordPivotSeatResult({ paths: {pivot_paths_json}, pivotId: '{pivot_id}', seat: {pivot_seat_001_json}, outcome }))}\\n`);\n952:                   EOF\n953:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n954: \n955:               step_dispatch_pivot_seat_002:\n956:                 action: \"Natively dispatch the critical research direction-selection seat\"\n957:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain 'seat-002'\"\n958:                 capture_timing: true\n959:                 if_native:\n960:                   dispatch:\n961:                     agent: deep-research\n962:                     model: opus\n963:                     context_source: \"pivot_seat_002_prompt\"\n964:                   wait_for_completion: true\n965:                 failure_contract: \"A native dispatch failure binds status=rejected, a {name,message} error, and the measured timestamps/duration, then proceeds to step_record_pivot_seat_002.\"\n966:                 outputs:\n967:                   - pivot_seat_002_dispatch_status: \"fulfilled or rejected\"\n968:                   - pivot_seat_002_output_json: \"Raw native return serialized as JSON when fulfilled\"\n969:                   - pivot_seat_002_error_json: \"{name,message} when rejected\"\n970:                   - pivot_seat_002_started_at_iso: \"Dispatch start timestamp\"\n971:                   - pivot_seat_002_completed_at_iso: \"Dispatch completion timestamp\"\n972:                   - pivot_seat_002_duration_ms: \"Dispatch duration in milliseconds\"\n973: \n974:               step_record_pivot_seat_002:\n975:                 action: \"Durably record the seat-002 native dispatch outcome\"\n976:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain 'seat-002'\"\n977:                 command: |\n978:                   node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n979:                   import { recordPivotSeatResult } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts';\n980:                   const status = '{pivot_seat_002_dispatch_status}';\n981:                   const outcome = status === 'fulfilled'\n982:                     ? { status, output: {pivot_seat_002_output_json}, startedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_002_started_at_iso}', completedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_002_completed_at_iso}', durationMs: Number('{pivot_seat_002_duration_ms}') }\n983:                     : { status: 'rejected', error: {pivot_seat_002_error_json}, startedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_002_started_at_iso}', completedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_002_completed_at_iso}', durationMs: Number('{pivot_seat_002_duration_ms}') };\n984:                   process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify(recordPivotSeatResult({ paths: {pivot_paths_json}, pivotId: '{pivot_id}', seat: {pivot_seat_002_json}, outcome }))}\\n`);\n985:                   EOF\n986:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n987: \n988:               step_dispatch_pivot_seat_003:\n989:                 action: \"Natively dispatch the pragmatic research direction-selection seat\"\n990:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain 'seat-003'\"\n991:                 capture_timing: true\n992:                 if_native:\n993:                   dispatch:\n994:                     agent: deep-research\n995:                     model: opus\n996:                     context_source: \"pivot_seat_003_prompt\"\n997:                   wait_for_completion: true\n998:                 failure_contract: \"A native dispatch failure binds status=rejected, a {name,message} error, and the measured timestamps/duration, then proceeds to step_record_pivot_seat_003.\"\n999:                 outputs:\n1000:                   - pivot_seat_003_dispatch_status: \"fulfilled or rejected\"\n1001:                   - pivot_seat_003_output_json: \"Raw native return serialized as JSON when fulfilled\"\n1002:                   - pivot_seat_003_error_json: \"{name,message} when rejected\"\n1003:                   - pivot_seat_003_started_at_iso: \"Dispatch start timestamp\"\n1004:                   - pivot_seat_003_completed_at_iso: \"Dispatch completion timestamp\"\n1005:                   - pivot_seat_003_duration_ms: \"Dispatch duration in milliseconds\"\n1006: \n1007:               step_record_pivot_seat_003:\n1008:                 action: \"Durably record the seat-003 native dispatch outcome\"\n1009:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain 'seat-003'\"\n1010:                 command: |\n1011:                   node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n1012:                   import { recordPivotSeatResult } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts';\n1013:                   const status = '{pivot_seat_003_dispatch_status}';\n1014:                   const outcome = status === 'fulfilled'\n1015:                     ? { status, output: {pivot_seat_003_output_json}, startedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_003_started_at_iso}', completedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_003_completed_at_iso}', durationMs: Number('{pivot_seat_003_duration_ms}') }\n1016:                     : { status: 'rejected', error: {pivot_seat_003_error_json}, startedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_003_started_at_iso}', completedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_003_completed_at_iso}', durationMs: Number('{pivot_seat_003_duration_ms}') };\n1017:                   process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify(recordPivotSeatResult({ paths: {pivot_paths_json}, pivotId: '{pivot_id}', seat: {pivot_seat_003_json}, outcome }))}\\n`);\n1018:                   EOF\n1019:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1020: \n1021:               step_finalize_divergent_pivot:\n1022:                 action: \"Finalize the prepared pivot after all missing native seats are durable\"\n1023:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending'\"\n1024:                 command: |\n1025:                   node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n1026:                   import { finalizePivotTransaction } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts';\n1027:                   process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify(finalizePivotTransaction({ paths: {pivot_paths_json}, pivotId: '{pivot_id}', resumed: {pivot_resumed} }))}\\n`);\n1028:                   EOF\n1029:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1030:                 outputs:\n1031:                   - pivot_finalize_json: \"The complete parsed final result\"\n1032: \n1033:               step_resolve_divergent_pivot_result:\n1034:                 action: \"Use prepare's terminal result on resume/short-circuit, otherwise use finalize's result\"\n1035:                 branch_on: \"pivot_prepare_status\"\n1036:                 if_pending: { bind: { pivot_result: \"{pivot_finalize_json}\" } }\n1037:                 if_completed_or_failed: { bind: { pivot_result: \"{pivot_prepare_json}\" } }\n1038: \n1039:               step_apply_divergent_pivot_result:\n1040:                 action: \"Adopt a successful focus or fail closed to the existing synthesis path\"\n1041:                 branch_on: \"pivot_result.status\"\n1042:                 if_completed:\n1043:                   set:\n1044:                     next_focus: \"{pivot_result.restoredFocus}\"\n1045:                     pivot_lineage: \"Pivot {pivot_result.pivotId} selected {pivot_result.selectedCandidate.id} from source iteration {current_iteration}.\"\n1046:                     saturated_directions: \"{pivot_result.completedEvent.saturatedDirections}\"\n1047:                   command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg}\"\n1048:                   log: \"Divergent pivot {pivot_result.pivotId} restored focus to {pivot_result.restoredFocus}; continuing iteration {current_iteration}.\"\n1049:                   proceed_to: step_rejected_pattern_cache\n1050:                 if_failed:\n1051:                   log: \"Divergent pivot {pivot_result.pivotId} failed closed ({pivot_result.failureReason}); proceeding to synthesis.\"\n1052:                   skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1053:             on_error:\n1054:               log: \"Divergent pivot integration error; failing closed to the existing synthesis path.\"\n1055:               skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1056:           if_existing_terminal_path:\n1057:             log: \"Loop stopping. Reason: {reason}\"\n1058:             skip_to: phase_synthesis\n1059:         if_stuck_recovery:\n1060:           append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"stuckRecovery\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"stopReason\":\"stuckRecovery\",\"fromIteration\":{current_iteration},\"outcome\":\"recovered\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n1061:           log: \"Stuck detected ({stuck_count} consecutive no-progress). Entering recovery.\"\n1062:           set: { next_focus: \"RECOVERY: Widen scope. Try fundamentally different approach. Least-explored question: {least_explored}\" }\n1063:           reset: { stuck_count: 0 }\n1064:         if_continue:\n1065:           log: \"Iteration {current_iteration}: Continuing. Focus: {next_focus}\"\n1066: \n1067:       step_rejected_pattern_cache:\n1068:         action: \"Apply reducer-derived rejected-pattern suppression before dispatch candidate selection\"\n1069:         read:\n1070:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1071:           - \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n1072:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1073:         candidate_sources:\n1074:           next_focus:\n1075:             category: \"next-focus\"\n1076:             values:\n1077:               - \"{next_focus}\"\n1078:               - \"{remaining_questions_list}\"\n1079:               - \"{carried_forward_open_questions}\"\n1080:           recovery:\n1081:             category: \"recovery\"\n1082:             values:\n1083:               - \"{recovery_strategy}\"\n1084:               - \"{least_explored}\"\n1085:           ideas:\n1086:             category: \"ideas\"\n1087:             values:\n1088:               - \"{promoted_ideas_list}\"\n1089:             optional_file: \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/research-ideas.md\"\n1090:         algorithm: |\n1091:           Use registry.rejectedPatternIndex and registry.promotedIdeas from the latest\n1092:           reducer pass as the source of truth.\n1093:           Compare normalized exact text first. Then compare fuzzy similarity with\n1094:           rejected_pattern_fuzzy_threshold, but only when candidate and rejected categories\n1095:           are compatible. Remove suppressed candidates from next_focus, recovery, and ideas\n1096:           selection before rendering the dispatch prompt. If all candidates are suppressed,\n1097:           halt for operator input instead of reusing a rejected idea.\n1098:         outputs:\n1099:           - accepted_next_focus: \"First unsuppressed next-focus candidate, or null\"\n1100:           - accepted_recovery_candidate: \"First unsuppressed recovery candidate, or null\"\n1101:           - accepted_idea_candidate: \"First unsuppressed ideas candidate, or null\"\n1102:           - rejected_candidate_matches: \"Suppressed candidate diagnostics from registry.suppressedCandidates plus any current-step matches\"\n1103:         if_next_focus_suppressed:\n1104:           set: { next_focus: \"{accepted_next_focus || accepted_recovery_candidate || accepted_idea_candidate}\" }\n1105:           log: \"Rejected-pattern cache suppressed the prior candidate; dispatching the next accepted candidate.\"\n1106:         if_all_candidates_suppressed:\n1107:           halt: true\n1108:           message: 'All next-focus, recovery, and ideas candidates match active rejected patterns. Remove or reset the rejected pattern, or provide a new focus. In a ledger-backed run (a deep-research-ledger/frames folder beside the state log) the next projection replaces a hand-edited state log, so record the removal or reset through the append gateway: write one row to a file, either {\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"idea_rejected_removed\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"pattern\":\"<rejected text>\",\"category\":\"<its category>\",\"timestamp\":\"<UTC now, e.g. 2026-05-24T00:00:00Z>\"} or {\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"idea_rejected_reset\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"reason\":\"<why>\",\"timestamp\":\"<UTC now>\"}, then run node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode research --run-directory {artifact_dir} --event-json <that file> and rerun the reducer before resuming.'\n1109: \n1110:       step_ideas_backlog_lifecycle:\n1111:         action: \"Track reducer-owned observed/promoted/rejected idea lifecycle before dispatch\"\n1112:         read:\n1113:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1114:           - \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n1115:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1116:         lifecycle:\n1117:           observed_event: \"idea_observed\"\n1118:           promoted_event: \"idea_promoted\"\n1119:           rejected_event: \"idea_rejected\"\n1120:           min_observations: \"{min_idea_observations}\"\n1121:           authority: \"Leaf agents emit observations only; reducer emits promotions and owns ranking.\"\n1122:         validate:\n1123:           - \"If new leaf-authored output includes idea_promoted, fail validation; only reducer output may append idea_promoted.\"\n1124:           - \"If promoted_ideas_count > 0 and next_focus is empty or all questions are resolved, prefer the first unsuppressed promoted idea.\"\n1125:           - \"If suppressed_ideas_count > 0, do not render those ideas into dispatch context.\"\n1126:         outputs:\n1127:           - observed_ideas_count: \"Reducer-derived observed ideas count\"\n1128:           - promoted_ideas_count: \"Reducer-derived promoted ideas count after minIdeaObservations\"\n1129:           - suppressed_ideas_count: \"Reducer-derived rejected/suppressed ideas count\"\n1130:           - accepted_idea_candidate: \"First unsuppressed promoted idea, or null\"\n1131: \n1132:       step_normalize_pause_events:\n1133:         action: \"Normalize pause and recovery lifecycle events to the frozen STOP_REASONS enum at emission time\"\n1134:         stop_reasons_enum: [converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused]\n1135:         rule_pause_sentinel:\n1136:           raw_event_forbidden: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"paused\"}'\n1137:           canonical_event: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"userPaused\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"stopReason\":\"userPaused\",\"sentinelPath\":\"{state_paths.pause_sentinel}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n1138:         rule_stuck_recovery:\n1139:           raw_event_forbidden: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"stuck_recovery\"}'\n1140:           canonical_event: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"stuckRecovery\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"stopReason\":\"stuckRecovery\",\"fromIteration\":{current_iteration},\"outcome\":\"recovered\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n1141: \n1142:       step_marker_scan:\n1143:         action: \"H-2 loop-prevention guard: scan previous iteration's rendered prompt for nested research marker\"\n1144:         canonical_header: \"DEEP-RESEARCH\"\n1145:         nested_marker_pattern: \"^(DEEP-REVIEW|CODE-REVIEW)$\"\n1146:         algorithm: |\n1147:           if current_iteration > 1:\n1148:             PREV_PROMPT_PATH = \"{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{previous_iteration}.md\"\n1149:             if file_exists(PREV_PROMPT_PATH):\n1150:               PREV_PROMPT_FIRST_LINE = head -1 of PREV_PROMPT_PATH\n1151:               if PREV_PROMPT_FIRST_LINE matches nested_marker_pattern:\n1152:                 log \"ERROR: nested research-of-review loop detected (review marker found in previous iteration prompt). Aborting.\"\n1153:                 halt with exit code 2\n1154:         note: |\n1155:           False-positive prevention: a research prompt that starts with its own canonical\n1156:           header is this loop's own iteration output, never a nested dispatch; only a review\n1157:           marker is, so the guard matches nested_marker_pattern rather than the canonical\n1158:           header. Markers appearing in comments or body text are ignored. True-positive\n1159:           triggers only when a previous iteration's rendered prompt literally starts with a\n1160:           review marker, indicating a nested research-of-review dispatch.\n1161: \n1162:       step_dispatch_iteration:\n1163:         action: \"Dispatch one iteration via the selected executor\"\n1164:         resolve_executor:\n1165:           source: \"config.executor\"\n1166:           loader: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts#parseExecutorConfig\"\n1167:         pre_dispatch:\n1168:           generate_summary: |\n1169:             STATE SUMMARY (auto-generated):\n1170:             Segment: {current_segment} | Iteration: {current_iteration} of {max_iterations}\n1171:             Questions: {answered_count}/{total_questions} answered | Last focus: {last_focus}\n1172:             Last 2 ratios: {ratio_prev} -> {ratio_latest} | Stuck count: {stuck_count}\n1173:             {resource_map_prompt_line}\n1174:             {lineage_context_prompt_line}\n1175:             Next focus: {next_focus}\n1176:           render_prompt_pack:\n1177:             template_path: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl\"\n1178:             renderer: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/prompt-pack.ts#renderPromptPack\"\n1179:             output_path: \"{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md\"\n1180:             variables:\n1181:               state_summary: \"{state_summary}\"\n1182:               research_topic: \"{research_topic}\"\n1183:               current_iteration: \"{current_iteration}\"\n1184:               max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n1185:               next_focus: \"{next_focus}\"\n1186:               remaining_questions_list: \"{remaining_questions_list}\"\n1187:               carried_forward_open_questions: \"{carried_forward_open_questions}\"\n1188:               last_3_summaries: \"{last_3_summaries}\"\n1189:               pivot_lineage: \"{pivot_lineage}\"\n1190:               saturated_directions: \"{saturated_directions}\"\n1191:               state_paths_config: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1192:               state_paths_state_log: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1193:               state_paths_strategy: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1194:               state_paths_registry: \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n1195:               state_paths_iteration_pattern: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1196:               state_paths_delta_pattern: \"{state_paths.delta_pattern}\"\n1197:         pre_dispatch_audit:\n1198:           skip_when: \"config.executor.type == 'native'\"\n1199:           call: \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts#writeFirstRecordExecutor\"\n1200:           args:\n1201:             stateLogPath: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1202:             executor: \"{config.executor}\"\n1203:             iteration: \"{current_iteration}\"\n1204:         branch_on: \"config.executor.type\"\n1205:         if_native:\n1206:           dispatch:\n1207:             agent: deep-research\n1208:             model: opus\n1209:             context_source: \"rendered_prompt_pack\"\n1210:           wait_for_completion: true\n1211:         if_cli_claude_code:\n1212:           command: |\n1213:             node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n1214:             import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n1215:             import { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\n1216: \n1217:             import { runAuditedExecutorCommand } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts';\n1218:             import { resolveClaudePermissionMode } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts';\n1219: \n1220:             const executor = {\n1221:               kind: 'cli-claude-code',\n1222:               model: '{config.executor.model}',\n1223:               reasoningEffort: '{config.executor.reasoningEffort}' === 'null' ? null : '{config.executor.reasoningEffort}',\n1224:               serviceTier: '{config.executor.serviceTier}' === 'null' ? null : '{config.executor.serviceTier}',\n1225:               sandboxMode: '{config.executor.sandboxMode}' === 'null' ? null : '{config.executor.sandboxMode}',\n1226:               timeoutSeconds: Number('{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}'),\n1227:             };\n1228:             const args = [\n1229:               '-p',\n1230:               readFileSync('{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md', 'utf8'),\n1231:               '--model',\n1232:               executor.model,\n1233:               '--permission-mode',\n1234:               resolveClaudePermissionMode(executor.sandboxMode),\n1235:               '--output-format',\n1236:               'text',\n1237:             ];\n1238:             if (executor.reasoningEffort) {\n1239:               args.push('--effort', executor.reasoningEffort);\n1240:             }\n1241: \n1242:             const dispatchFacts = {\n1243:               command: 'deep/research',\n1244:               mode: 'research',\n1245:               specFolder: '{spec_folder}',\n1246:               artifactDir: '{state_paths.packet_dir}',\n1247:               iteration: Number('{current_iteration}'),\n1248:               executorKind: '{config.executor.type}',\n1249:               branchId: '{config.executor.type}',\n1250:               sessionId: '{config.lineage.sessionId}',\n1251:               generation: Number('{config.lineage.generation}'),\n1252:             };\n1253:             const dispatchId = 'research-i{current_iteration}-g{config.lineage.generation}';\n1254:             process.exit(\n1255:               runAuditedExecutorCommand({\n1256:                 command: 'claude',\n1257:                 args,\n1258:                 cwd: '{repo_root}',\n1259:                 timeoutSeconds: executor.timeoutSeconds,\n1260:                 stateLogPath: '{state_paths.state_log}',\n1261:                 executor,\n1262:                 iteration: Number('{current_iteration}'),\n1263:                 receiptDir: '{state_paths.packet_dir}/dispatch-receipts',\n1264:                 dispatchId,\n1265:               }),\n1266:             );\n1267:             EOF\n1268:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1269:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1270:           wait_for_completion: true\n1271:           notes:\n1272:             - \"sandboxMode maps to permission-mode: read-only -> plan, workspace-write -> acceptEdits, danger-full-access -> bypassPermissions\"\n1273:             - \"claude-code has no serviceTier flag\"\n1274:             - \"claude-code supports --effort for reasoning depth\"\n1275:         if_cli_cursor:\n1276:           command: |\n1277:             node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n1278:             import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n1279:             import { createRequire } from 'node:module';\n1280:             import { runAuditedExecutorCommand } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts';\n1281:             import { resolveSandboxMode, resolveClaudePermissionMode } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts';\n1282:             import {\n1283:               snapshotOutOfScopeDirtyPaths,\n1284:               enforceWriteContainment,\n1285:             } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/write-containment.ts';\n1286: \n1287:             // cursor-agent/devin/pi have no single-executor branch of their own, so\n1288:             // without this they silently degrade to native. The command builder is the\n1289:             // same one the fan-out lineage path uses, so the enforced model allowlist,\n1290:             // headless write-mode flags, and binary preflight stay one source of truth.\n1291:             // It throws (fail closed) when the binary is absent or the model is off the\n1292:             // allowlist, so a requested CLI executor never becomes native.\n1293:             const require = createRequire(import.meta.url);\n1294:             const { buildLineageCommand } = require('./.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs');\n1295: \n1296:             const kind = '{config.executor.type}';\n1297:             const model = '{config.executor.model}' === 'null' ? null : '{config.executor.model}';\n1298:             const timeoutSeconds = Number('{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}');\n1299:             // The iteration must write its own iteration file, delta and state record,\n1300:             // so the leaf runs workspace-write; the builder maps that to each CLI's real\n1301:             // write-permitting headless flags.\n1302:             const sandboxMode = 'workspace-write';\n1303:             const lineage = { kind, model, sandboxMode };\n1304:             const resolvedSandbox = resolveSandboxMode(sandboxMode);\n1305:             const resolvedPermission = resolveClaudePermissionMode(sandboxMode);\n1306: \n1307:             const repoRoot = '{repo_root}';\n1308:             const promptBody = readFileSync('{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md', 'utf8');\n1309:             const { command, args, input } = buildLineageCommand(\n1310:               lineage,\n1311:               promptBody,\n1312:               resolvedSandbox,\n1313:               resolvedPermission,\n1314:               { env: process.env, cwd: repoRoot },\n1315:             );\n1316: \n1317:             const executor = {\n1318:               kind,\n1319:               model,\n1320:               configDir: null,\n1321:               reasoningEffort: null,\n1322:               serviceTier: null,\n1323:               sandboxMode,\n1324:               timeoutSeconds,\n1325:               governor: null,\n1326:             };\n1327:             const dispatchId = 'research-i{current_iteration}-g{generation}';\n1328:             const artifactDir = '{artifact_dir}';\n1329:             const preDispatchDirtyPaths = snapshotOutOfScopeDirtyPaths({ repoRoot, artifactDir });\n1330:             const dispatchExit = runAuditedExecutorCommand({\n1331:               command,\n1332:               args,\n1333:               cwd: repoRoot,\n1334:               timeoutSeconds,\n1335:               stateLogPath: '{state_paths.state_log}',\n1336:               executor,\n1337:               iteration: Number('{current_iteration}'),\n1338:               input,\n1339:               receiptDir: '{state_paths.packet_dir}/dispatch-receipts',\n1340:               dispatchId,\n1341:             });\n1342:             const containment = enforceWriteContainment({\n1343:               repoRoot,\n1344:               artifactDir,\n1345:               preDispatchDirtyPaths,\n1346:               stateLogPath: '{state_paths.state_log}',\n1347:               iteration: Number('{current_iteration}'),\n1348:               label: dispatchId,\n1349:             });\n1350:             if (containment.violations.length > 0) {\n1351:               console.error(\n1352:                 'write-containment advisory: detected ' + containment.violations.length\n1353:                   + ' out-of-scope path(s), left on disk: '\n1354:                   + containment.violations.map((v) => v.path).join(', '),\n1355:               );\n1356:             }\n1357:             process.exit(dispatchExit);\n1358:             EOF\n1359:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1360:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1361:           wait_for_completion: true\n1362:           notes:\n1363:             - \"cli-cursor single-executor: dispatches per-iteration through the shared fan-out command builder (buildLineageCommand) so the enforced cli-cursor model allowlist + headless write flags stay one source of truth; runAuditedExecutorCommand emits INTENT + COMPLETION receipts\"\n1364:             - \"Fails closed when cursor-agent is absent or the model is off the allowlist (buildLineageCommand throws, exit non-zero) — a requested cli-cursor executor never degrades to native\"\n1365:         if_cli_devin:\n1366:           command: |\n1367:             node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n1368:             import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n1369:             import { createRequire } from 'node:module';\n1370:             import { runAuditedExecutorCommand } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts';\n1371:             import { resolveSandboxMode, resolveClaudePermissionMode } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts';\n1372:             import {\n1373:               snapshotOutOfScopeDirtyPaths,\n1374:               enforceWriteContainment,\n1375:             } from './.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/write-containment.ts';\n1376: \n1377:             // cursor-agent/devin/pi have no single-executor branch of their own, so\n1378:             // without this they silently degrade to native. The command builder is the\n1379:             // same one the fan-out lineage path uses, so the enforced model allowlist,\n1380:             // headless write-mode flags, and binary preflight stay one source of truth.\n1381:             // It throws (fail closed) when the binary is absent or the model is off the\n1382:             // allowlist, so a requested CLI executor never becomes native.\n1383:             const require = createRequire(import.meta.url);\n1384:             const { buildLineageCommand } = require('./.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs');\n1385: \n1386:             const kind = '{config.executor.type}';\n1387:             const model = '{config.executor.model}' === 'null' ? null : '{config.executor.model}';\n1388:             const timeoutSeconds = Number('{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}');\n1389:             // The iteration must write its own iteration file, delta and state record,\n1390:             // so the leaf runs workspace-write; the builder maps that to each CLI's real\n1391:             // write-permitting headless flags.\n1392:             const sandboxMode = 'workspace-write';\n1393:             const lineage = { kind, model, sandboxMode };\n1394:             const resolvedSandbox = resolveSandboxMode(sandboxMode);\n1395:             const resolvedPermission = resolveClaudePermissionMode(sandboxMode);\n1396: \n1397:             const repoRoot = '{repo_root}';\n1398:             const promptBody = readFileSync('{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md', 'utf8');\n1399:             const { command, args, input } = buildLineageCommand(\n1400:               lineage,\n1401:               promptBody,\n1402:               resolvedSandbox,\n1403:               resolvedPermission,\n1404:               { env: process.env, cwd: repoRoot },\n1405:             );\n1406: \n1407:             const executor = {\n1408:               kind,\n1409:               model,\n1410:               configDir: null,\n1411:               reasoningEffort: null,\n1412:               serviceTier: null,\n1413:               sandboxMode,\n1414:               timeoutSeconds,\n1415:               governor: null,\n1416:             };\n1417:             const dispatchId = 'research-i{current_iteration}-g{generation}';\n1418:             const artifactDir = '{artifact_dir}';\n1419:             const preDispatchDirtyPaths = snapshotOutOfScopeDirtyPaths({ repoRoot, artifactDir });\n1420:             const dispatchExit = runAuditedExecutorCommand({\n1421:               command,\n1422:               args,\n1423:               cwd: repoRoot,\n1424:               timeoutSeconds,\n1425:               stateLogPath: '{state_paths.state_log}',\n1426:               executor,\n1427:               iteration: Number('{current_iteration}'),\n1428:               input,\n1429:               receiptDir: '{state_paths.packet_dir}/dispatch-receipts',\n1430:               dispatchId,\n1431:             });\n1432:             const containment = enforceWriteContainment({\n1433:               repoRoot,\n1434:               artifactDir,\n1435:               preDispatchDirtyPaths,\n1436:               stateLogPath: '{state_paths.state_log}',\n1437:               iteration: Number('{current_iteration}'),\n1438:               label: dispatchId,\n1439:             });\n1440:             if (containment.violations.length > 0) {\n1441:               console.error(\n1442:                 'write-containment advisory: detected ' + containment.violations.length\n1443:                   + ' out-of-scope path(s), left on disk: '\n1444:                   + containment.violations.map((v) => v.path).join(', '),\n1445:               );\n1446:             }\n1447:             process.exit(dispatchExit);\n1448:             EOF\n1449:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1450:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 1451]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml\", \"offset\": 751, \"limit\": 700}"},"time":{"start":1793094371197,"end":1793094372679}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793094372680,"sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","part":{"partID":"prt_17cc0cb55001ZLiBxYOND0w9nY","sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","messageID":"msg_17cc0b9a7001rZJNdVAycSyQdm","type":"tool","id":"call_1472678bbdcb4d4d2eb8e2ee","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md, lines 1-188\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Research Strategy Template\n3: description: Runtime template copied to research/ during initialization to track research progress, focus decisions, and outcomes across iterations.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep research strategy\"\n6:   - \"research strategy template\"\n7:   - \"research session tracking\"\n8:   - \"exhausted research approaches\"\n9:   - \"research stop conditions\"\n10:   - \"ruled out research directions\"\n11: importance_tier: normal\n12: contextType: planning\n13: version: 1.14.0.19\n14: ---\n15: \n16: # Deep Research Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n17: \n18: Runtime template copied to `{spec_folder}/research/` during initialization. Tracks research progress across iterations.\n19: \n20: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n21: \n22: ### Purpose\n23: \n24: Serves as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep research session. Records what to investigate, what worked, what failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n25: \n26: ### Usage\n27: \n28: - **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{spec_folder}/research/deep-research-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Key Questions, Known Context, and Research Boundaries from config and memory context.\n29: - **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, writes iteration evidence, and the reducer refreshes What Worked/Failed, answered questions, carried-forward questions, ruled-out directions, and Next Focus.\n30: - **Mutability:** Mutable — analyst-owned sections remain stable, while machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer after each iteration. Section 3 is a generated projection from the reducer registry.\n31: - **Protection:** Shared state with explicit ownership boundaries. Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n32: \n33: ### Question Injection Surface\n34: \n35: Use `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl` to append external questions during an active run. Each line is one JSON object with:\n36: \n37: - `id`: stable inbox record identifier\n38: - `text`: question text to promote\n39: - `source`: concrete source label, such as an angle bank entry, analyst strategy, or operator note\n40: - `origin`: one of `angle-bank`, `analyst-strategy`, `operator`, or `legacy-import`\n41: - `injectedAtIteration`: iteration number when the question was introduced\n42: - `promotedQuestionId`: promoted registry question id, or `null` until promotion\n43: \n44: The reducer reads the inbox on every reduce step and carries `origin` into the question registry and dashboard badges. Direct edits to Section 3 still work as a compatibility path, but they are attributed as `legacy-import`.\n45: \n46: Question ownership is explicit:\n47: \n48: - Inbox rows are immutable input.\n49: - The reducer registry is canonical question state.\n50: - Section 3 is rendered only from the registry view.\n51: \n52: When an inbox row targets an existing registry question but carries different text, the reducer keeps the registry value, records `operatorDecision: needs_decision`, and appends a `question_conflict` event with both `inboxValue` and `registryValue`.\n53: \n54: ---\n55: \n56: ## 2. TOPIC\n57: [Research topic from config -- set during initialization]\n58: \n59: ---\n60: \n61: <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n62: ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n63: Generated from the reducer registry. Add external or late questions through `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl`; direct edits are imported as compatibility input and may be replaced on the next reduce step.\n64: \n65: - [ ] [Question 1 -- identified during initialization or iteration 1]\n66: - [ ] [Question 2]\n67: - [ ] [Question 3]\n68: <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n69: \n70: ---\n71: \n72: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n73: [What this research session is NOT trying to answer -- populated during initialization]\n74: \n75: ---\n76: \n77: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n78: [Explicit conditions beyond convergence that should end the session -- populated during initialization]\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: <!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n83: ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n84: [None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n85: <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n86: \n87: ---\n88: \n89: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n90: <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n91: ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n92: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n93: - [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n94: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n95: \n96: ---\n97: \n98: <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n99: ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n100: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n101: - [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n102: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n103: \n104: ---\n105: \n106: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n107: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n108: [Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n109: \n110: ### [Category Name] -- BLOCKED (iteration N, N attempts)\n111: - What was tried: [specific approaches attempted]\n112: - Why blocked: [root cause of exhaustion]\n113: - Do NOT retry: [explicit prohibition]\n114: \n115: ### [Category Name] -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration N)\n116: - What worked: [successful approaches in this category]\n117: - Prefer for: [related questions where this category may help]\n118: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n119: \n120: ---\n121: \n122: <!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n123: ## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n124: [Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n125: - [Approach]: [Why ruled out] (iteration N, evidence: [source])\n126: <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n127: \n128: ---\n129: \n130: <!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n131: ## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n132: - Completed pivots: 0\n133: - Failed pivots: 0\n134: - Audited overrides: 0\n135: - Saturated: none yet\n136: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n137: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n138: <!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n139: \n140: ---\n141: \n142: <!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n143: ## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n144: [Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n145: <!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n146: \n147: ---\n148: \n149: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n150: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n151: [Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration]\n152: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n153: \n154: ---\n155: \n156: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n157: ## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n158: [Populated during initialization from the continuity ladder and ripgrep recipes, if any prior work exists]\n159: \n160: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n161: \n162: Populate during initialization when the target is codebase-scoped. Keep this pointer-based and small:\n163: \n164: - Source pointers: paths, symbols, or resource-map entries relevant to the topic.\n165: - Reuse candidates: existing utilities, patterns, docs, or agents worth extending.\n166: - Integration points: files or contracts the research is likely to touch.\n167: - Constraints and risks: scope limits, stale graph or memory gaps, and known non-goals.\n168: \n169: Do not inline full source bodies. Do not dispatch the retired standalone context loop. Use `@context` for one-shot retrieval, and use this snapshot only to seed the research loop.\n170: \n171: ---\n172: \n173: ## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n174: - Max iterations: [from config]\n175: - Convergence threshold: [from config]\n176: - Per-iteration budget: [from config.maxToolCallsPerIteration] tool calls, [from config.maxMinutesPerIteration] minutes\n177: - Progressive synthesis: true (default)\n178: - research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n179: - Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred, not runtime-wired)\n180: - Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A, including Section 10A pivot lineage\n181: - Question injection surface: `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl`\n182: - Question conflict owner: reducer registry; `question_conflict` events surface inbox/registry disagreements for operator decision\n183: - Canonical pause sentinel: `research/.deep-research-pause`\n184: - Capability matrix: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/runtime-capabilities.json`\n185: - Capability matrix doc: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/guides/capability-matrix.md`\n186: - Capability resolver: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs`\n187: - Current generation: [from config.lineage.generation]\n188: - Started: [timestamp]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md, lines 1-188\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Research Strategy Template\n3: description: Runtime template copied to research/ during initialization to track research progress, focus decisions, and outcomes across iterations.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep research strategy\"\n6:   - \"research strategy template\"\n7:   - \"research session tracking\"\n8:   - \"exhausted research approaches\"\n9:   - \"research stop conditions\"\n10:   - \"ruled out research directions\"\n11: importance_tier: normal\n12: contextType: planning\n13: version: 1.14.0.19\n14: ---\n15: \n16: # Deep Research Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n17: \n18: Runtime template copied to `{spec_folder}/research/` during initialization. Tracks research progress across iterations.\n19: \n20: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n21: \n22: ### Purpose\n23: \n24: Serves as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep research session. Records what to investigate, what worked, what failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n25: \n26: ### Usage\n27: \n28: - **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{spec_folder}/research/deep-research-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Key Questions, Known Context, and Research Boundaries from config and memory context.\n29: - **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, writes iteration evidence, and the reducer refreshes What Worked/Failed, answered questions, carried-forward questions, ruled-out directions, and Next Focus.\n30: - **Mutability:** Mutable — analyst-owned sections remain stable, while machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer after each iteration. Section 3 is a generated projection from the reducer registry.\n31: - **Protection:** Shared state with explicit ownership boundaries. Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n32: \n33: ### Question Injection Surface\n34: \n35: Use `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl` to append external questions during an active run. Each line is one JSON object with:\n36: \n37: - `id`: stable inbox record identifier\n38: - `text`: question text to promote\n39: - `source`: concrete source label, such as an angle bank entry, analyst strategy, or operator note\n40: - `origin`: one of `angle-bank`, `analyst-strategy`, `operator`, or `legacy-import`\n41: - `injectedAtIteration`: iteration number when the question was introduced\n42: - `promotedQuestionId`: promoted registry question id, or `null` until promotion\n43: \n44: The reducer reads the inbox on every reduce step and carries `origin` into the question registry and dashboard badges. Direct edits to Section 3 still work as a compatibility path, but they are attributed as `legacy-import`.\n45: \n46: Question ownership is explicit:\n47: \n48: - Inbox rows are immutable input.\n49: - The reducer registry is canonical question state.\n50: - Section 3 is rendered only from the registry view.\n51: \n52: When an inbox row targets an existing registry question but carries different text, the reducer keeps the registry value, records `operatorDecision: needs_decision`, and appends a `question_conflict` event with both `inboxValue` and `registryValue`.\n53: \n54: ---\n55: \n56: ## 2. TOPIC\n57: [Research topic from config -- set during initialization]\n58: \n59: ---\n60: \n61: <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n62: ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n63: Generated from the reducer registry. Add external or late questions through `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl`; direct edits are imported as compatibility input and may be replaced on the next reduce step.\n64: \n65: - [ ] [Question 1 -- identified during initialization or iteration 1]\n66: - [ ] [Question 2]\n67: - [ ] [Question 3]\n68: <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n69: \n70: ---\n71: \n72: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n73: [What this research session is NOT trying to answer -- populated during initialization]\n74: \n75: ---\n76: \n77: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n78: [Explicit conditions beyond convergence that should end the session -- populated during initialization]\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: <!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n83: ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n84: [None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n85: <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n86: \n87: ---\n88: \n89: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n90: <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n91: ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n92: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n93: - [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n94: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n95: \n96: ---\n97: \n98: <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n99: ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n100: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n101: - [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n102: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n103: \n104: ---\n105: \n106: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n107: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n108: [Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n109: \n110: ### [Category Name] -- BLOCKED (iteration N, N attempts)\n111: - What was tried: [specific approaches attempted]\n112: - Why blocked: [root cause of exhaustion]\n113: - Do NOT retry: [explicit prohibition]\n114: \n115: ### [Category Name] -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration N)\n116: - What worked: [successful approaches in this category]\n117: - Prefer for: [related questions where this category may help]\n118: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n119: \n120: ---\n121: \n122: <!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n123: ## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n124: [Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n125: - [Approach]: [Why ruled out] (iteration N, evidence: [source])\n126: <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n127: \n128: ---\n129: \n130: <!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n131: ## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n132: - Completed pivots: 0\n133: - Failed pivots: 0\n134: - Audited overrides: 0\n135: - Saturated: none yet\n136: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n137: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n138: <!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n139: \n140: ---\n141: \n142: <!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n143: ## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n144: [Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n145: <!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n146: \n147: ---\n148: \n149: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n150: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n151: [Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration]\n152: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n153: \n154: ---\n155: \n156: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n157: ## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n158: [Populated during initialization from the continuity ladder and ripgrep recipes, if any prior work exists]\n159: \n160: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n161: \n162: Populate during initialization when the target is codebase-scoped. Keep this pointer-based and small:\n163: \n164: - Source pointers: paths, symbols, or resource-map entries relevant to the topic.\n165: - Reuse candidates: existing utilities, patterns, docs, or agents worth extending.\n166: - Integration points: files or contracts the research is likely to touch.\n167: - Constraints and risks: scope limits, stale graph or memory gaps, and known non-goals.\n168: \n169: Do not inline full source bodies. Do not dispatch the retired standalone context loop. Use `@context` for one-shot retrieval, and use this snapshot only to seed the research loop.\n170: \n171: ---\n172: \n173: ## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n174: - Max iterations: [from config]\n175: - Convergence threshold: [from config]\n176: - Per-iteration budget: [from config.maxToolCallsPerIteration] tool calls, [from config.maxMinutesPerIteration] minutes\n177: - Progressive synthesis: true (default)\n178: - research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n179: - Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred, not runtime-wired)\n180: - Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A, including Section 10A pivot lineage\n181: - Question injection surface: `{spec_folder}/research/inbox.jsonl`\n182: - Question conflict owner: reducer registry; `question_conflict` events surface inbox/registry disagreements for operator decision\n183: - Canonical pause sentinel: `research/.deep-research-pause`\n184: - Capability matrix: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/runtime-capabilities.json`\n185: - Capability matrix doc: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/guides/capability-matrix.md`\n186: - Capability resolver: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs`\n187: - Current generation: [from config.lineage.generation]\n188: - Started: [timestamp]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793094372181,"end":1793094372680}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793094372682,"sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","part":{"partID":"prt_17cc0c914001tocI3M8fNbMp2Y","sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","messageID":"msg_17cc0b9a7001rZJNdVAycSyQdm","type":"tool","id":"call_98e496667afd1fed399794e0","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-config.json"},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-config.json, lines 1-83\n1: {\n2:   \"topic\": \"\",\n3:   \"maxIterations\": 10,\n4:   \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.05,\n5:   \"antiConvergence\": {\n6:     \"minIterations\": 3,\n7:     \"convergenceMode\": \"default\",\n8:     \"stopPolicy\": \"fail-closed\"\n9:   },\n10:   \"stuckThreshold\": 3,\n11:   \"maxDurationMinutes\": 120,\n12:   \"maxToolCallsPerIteration\": 24,\n13:   \"maxMinutesPerIteration\": 10,\n14:   \"progressiveSynthesis\": true,\n15:   \"specFolder\": \"\",\n16:   \"createdAt\": \"\",\n17:   \"status\": \"initialized\",\n18:   \"executionMode\": \"auto\",\n19:   \"executor\": {\n20:     \"kind\": \"native\",\n21:     \"model\": null,\n22:     \"reasoningEffort\": null,\n23:     \"serviceTier\": null,\n24:     \"sandboxMode\": null,\n25:     \"timeoutSeconds\": 900\n26:   },\n27:   \"lineage\": {\n28:     \"sessionId\": \"\",\n29:     \"parentSessionId\": null,\n30:     \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n31:     \"allowedModes\": [\n32:       \"new\",\n33:       \"resume\",\n34:       \"restart\"\n35:     ],\n36:     \"deferredModes\": [\n37:       \"fork\",\n38:       \"completed-continue\"\n39:     ],\n40:     \"generation\": 1,\n41:     \"continuedFromRun\": null\n42:   },\n43:   \"reducer\": {\n44:     \"enabled\": true,\n45:     \"version\": \"1.0\",\n46:     \"registryFile\": \"research/findings-registry.json\",\n47:     \"dashboardFile\": \"research/deep-research-dashboard.md\",\n48:     \"strategyFile\": \"research/deep-research-strategy.md\",