{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793094768580,"sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","part":{"partID":"prt_17cc697bf001KCMVSYO589GuHT","sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","messageID":"msg_17cc68e4f001HEk52pUOsBzaGc","type":"tool","id":"call_1731261ad6125e9ac3d3478a","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - fsmonitor daemon pile-up and worktree relocation regression\ndescription: Session tracking for the llmgateway-flash-undated-run2 fan-out lineage of the fsmonitor daemon research packet.\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\n---\n\n# Deep Research Strategy - Session Tracking\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nPersistent brain for the `llmgateway-flash-undated-run2` lineage. Records what to investigate, what worked, what failed, and where to focus next, so each iteration starts from files rather than memory.\n\n### Usage\n\n- **Init:** populated from the research topic and `scratch/findings.md` section 8.\n- **Per iteration:** the leaf reads Next Focus, writes iteration evidence, and the reducer refreshes the machine-owned sections.\n- **Mutability:** analyst-owned sections stay stable; machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer after each iteration.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nRoot-cause and fix design for git fsmonitor daemon pile-up and hangs in this repo: why the main checkout fsmonitor daemon stopped answering IPC and stalled a pre-push hook for 30 minutes, why 11 daemons accumulate across nested worktrees, what regressed sk-git/026 worktree relocation and reaper daemon handling, and how to prevent old daemons from running on. Start from `specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/scratch/findings.md` and answer its section 8 questions.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] Q1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default?\n- [ ] Q2. What is git 2.50.1's documented fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS, and how do fsmonitor.socketDir, idle shutdown and git fsmonitor--daemon stop behave when the daemon is wedged?\n- [ ] Q3. Is event overload the real cause of the hang, or is there a known daemon deadlock in this git version, for example around --ipc-threads or the cookie-file handshake?\n- [ ] Q4. Which call sites in the repo's hooks and scripts run git without a timeout, and which of them should opt out of fsmonitor?\n- [ ] Q5. What is the safest default: fsmonitor on with worktrees outside the checkout, or fsmonitor off for the main checkout and on per worktree?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Do not implement the fix in this packet; this is research and fix design only.\n- Do not re-litigate sk-git/026's completed worktree-pruning outcome beyond what explains the regression.\n- Do not benchmark filesystem watcher implementations other than git's built-in fsmonitor daemon.\n- Do not redesign the pre-push hook's unrelated gates.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- All five section-8 questions carry a cited answer or an explicit UNKNOWN with the check that would resolve it.\n- Additional stop condition: `maxIterations` (3) reached, because the dispatcher set `stopPolicy: max-iterations`.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n- [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n- [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n[Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nQ1: the sk-git/026 regression -- what unset `speckit.worktreeBase` and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and whether anything still defaults worktrees to `.worktrees/`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\nPrior evidence lives in `specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/scratch/findings.md` (symptom, blocked stack, daemon census, sk-git/026 regression evidence, candidate fixes). The completed packet `specs/sk-git/026-worktree-hygiene-and-relocation` records the original relocation and reaper work. Key live facts to re-verify rather than inherit: `core.fsmonitor=true` and `core.untrackedCache=true` in shared `.git/config`; `speckit.worktreeBase` unset; worktrees under `Public/.worktrees/`; a population of `git fsmonitor--daemon run --detach --ipc-threads=8` processes.\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Source pointers: `.skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh`, `.skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh`, `.skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh`, `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/generate-leaf-manifest.cjs`, `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs`, `~/.config/git/hooks/pre-push`.\n- Reuse candidates: the repo's existing fsmonitor opt-out convention (if any), the worktree reaper's published invariants, the sk-git/026 implementation summary.\n- Integration points: pre-push hook chain, worktree launch wrapper, reaper CLI, shared `.git/config` keys.\n- Constraints and risks: index-reading git commands can hang on the wedged daemon and can write the index; research must stay read-only and prefer `git log`/`git show`/`git config` reads.\n\n---\n\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n- Max iterations: 3\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: false (synthesis owns research.md at the end)\n- research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred, not runtime-wired)\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A, including Section 10A pivot lineage\n- Question injection surface: `research/inbox.jsonl` (not used in this lineage)\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `.deep-research-pause`\n- Capability matrix: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/runtime-capabilities.json`\n- Capability matrix doc: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/guides/capability-matrix.md`\n- Capability resolver: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs`\n- Current generation: 1\n- Started: 2026-10-27T09:52:14Z\n","path":"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-undated-run2/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-undated-run2/deep-research-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-undated-run2/deep-research-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"---\\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - fsmonitor daemon pile-up and worktree relocation regression\\ndescription: Session tracking for the llmgateway-flash-undated-run2 fan-out lineage of the fsmonitor daemon research packet.\\nimportance_tier: normal\\ncontextType: planning\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Research Strategy - Session Tracking\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nPersistent brain for the `llmgateway-flash-undated-run2` lineage. Records what to investigate, what worked, what failed, and where to focus next, so each iteration starts from files rather than memory.\\n\\n### Usage\\n\\n- **Init:** populated from the research topic and `scratch/findings.md` section 8.\\n- **Per iteration:** the leaf reads Next Focus, writes iteration evidence, and the reducer refreshes the machine-owned sections.\\n- **Mutability:** analyst-owned sections stay stable; machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer after each iteration.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nRoot-cause and fix design for git fsmonitor daemon pile-up and hangs in this repo: why the main checkout fsmonitor daemon stopped answering IPC and stalled a pre-push hook for 30 minutes, why 11 daemons accumulate across nested worktrees, what regressed sk-git/026 worktree relocation and reaper daemon handling, and how to prevent old daemons from running on. Start from `specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/scratch/findings.md` and answer its section 8 questions.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\\n- [ ] Q1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default?\\n- [ ] Q2. What is git 2.50.1's documented fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS, and how do fsmonitor.socketDir, idle shutdown and git fsmonitor--daemon stop behave when the daemon is wedged?\\n- [ ] Q3. Is event overload the real cause of the hang, or is there a known daemon deadlock in this git version, for example around --ipc-threads or the cookie-file handshake?\\n- [ ] Q4. Which call sites in the repo's hooks and scripts run git without a timeout, and which of them should opt out of fsmonitor?\\n- [ ] Q5. What is the safest default: fsmonitor on with worktrees outside the checkout, or fsmonitor off for the main checkout and on per worktree?\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- Do not implement the fix in this packet; this is research and fix design only.\\n- Do not re-litigate sk-git/026's completed worktree-pruning outcome beyond what explains the regression.\\n- Do not benchmark filesystem watcher implementations other than git's built-in fsmonitor daemon.\\n- Do not redesign the pre-push hook's unrelated gates.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- All five section-8 questions carry a cited answer or an explicit UNKNOWN with the check that would resolve it.\\n- Additional stop condition: `maxIterations` (3) reached, because the dispatcher set `stopPolicy: max-iterations`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n- [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n- [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Saturated: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\\n[Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\\nQ1: the sk-git/026 regression -- what unset `speckit.worktreeBase` and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and whether anything still defaults worktrees to `.worktrees/`.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\nPrior evidence lives in `specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/scratch/findings.md` (symptom, blocked stack, daemon census, sk-git/026 regression evidence, candidate fixes). The completed packet `specs/sk-git/026-worktree-hygiene-and-relocation` records the original relocation and reaper work. Key live facts to re-verify rather than inherit: `core.fsmonitor=true` and `core.untrackedCache=true` in shared `.git/config`; `speckit.worktreeBase` unset; worktrees under `Public/.worktrees/`; a population of `git fsmonitor--daemon run --detach --ipc-threads=8` processes.\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- Source pointers: `.skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh`, `.skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh`, `.skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh`, `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/generate-leaf-manifest.cjs`, `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs`, `~/.config/git/hooks/pre-push`.\\n- Reuse candidates: the repo's existing fsmonitor opt-out convention (if any), the worktree reaper's published invariants, the sk-git/026 implementation summary.\\n- Integration points: pre-push hook chain, worktree launch wrapper, reaper CLI, shared `.git/config` keys.\\n- Constraints and risks: index-reading git commands can hang on the wedged daemon and can write the index; research must stay read-only and prefer `git log`/`git show`/`git config` reads.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\\n- Max iterations: 3\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\\n- Progressive synthesis: false (synthesis owns research.md at the end)\\n- research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred, not runtime-wired)\\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A, including Section 10A pivot lineage\\n- Question injection surface: `research/inbox.jsonl` (not used in this lineage)\\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `.deep-research-pause`\\n- Capability matrix: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/runtime-capabilities.json`\\n- Capability matrix doc: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/guides/capability-matrix.md`\\n- Capability resolver: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/runtime-capabilities.cjs`\\n- Current generation: 1\\n- Started: 2026-10-27T09:52:14Z\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-undated-run2/deep-research-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793094752191,"end":1793094768580}}}}
