{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793094822394,"sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","part":{"partID":"prt_17cc79e83001Wacj9PsEnMsY50","sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","messageID":"msg_17cc78bda001fZCfmRI6byG4l5","type":"tool","id":"call_134aaeea46ea04197a63a55c","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public && echo \"=== deletion diff (daemon-related) ===\" && git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh | grep -E \"^[-+].*(daemon|DAEMON|orphan|ORPHAN|context-server)\" | head -30; echo \"=== commit dates ===\" && git log -1 --format=\"%h %ad %s\" --date=short a69a621a39a && git log -1 --format=\"%h %ad %s\" --date=short f83952c3a94 && git log -1 --format=\"%h %ad %s\" --date=short 3c7c3f83874; echo \"=== README invariant ===\" && sed -n '160,175p' .skilled/bin/README.md; echo \"=== daemon start times ===\" && ps -Ao pid,lstart,command | grep \"[f]smonitor--daemon run\" | awk '{print $1, $2, $3, $4, $5, $6}' | head -14"},"output":"=== deletion diff (daemon-related) ===\n-# Prune finished per-session AI worktrees, report orphan daemons.\n-# Companion to worktree-session.sh. Keeps .worktrees/ and the MCP daemon population\n-#   - REPORT (does not kill) MCP daemons whose recorded lease points at a .worktrees/ dir\n-#   --reap-daemons   Also SIGTERM (then SIGKILL) daemons whose worktree DB dir is gone.\n-#                    Off by default — daemon killing is opt-in to protect live sessions.\n-# checkout. Never kills a daemon whose worktree still exists.\n-REAP_DAEMONS=0\n-    --reap-daemons) REAP_DAEMONS=1 ;;\n-# Extract the worktree path a daemon cmdline points at, but only when it sits\n-_daemon_worktree_path_from_cmdline() {\n-_daemon_cmdline_is_orphan() {\n-  if ! worktree_path=\"$(_daemon_worktree_path_from_cmdline \"$cmdline\")\"; then\n-# 5. ORPHAN DAEMON REPORTING\n-# --- orphan daemon reporting (kill only with --reap-daemons) ---------------\n-# A worktree daemon writes its lease under <worktree-db-dir>/.system-spec-memory-launcher.json.\n-# If that lease names a live childPid but the worktree DB dir is gone, it is orphaned.\n-log \"scanning for orphan worktree daemons\"\n-ORPHANS=0\n-# is gone, so we instead detect live daemon PIDs whose cwd/db-dir no longer resolves.\n-# Conservative heuristic: list node daemons referencing a .worktrees/ path that is absent.\n-    *node*context-server.js*) ;;\n-  if ! _daemon_cmdline_is_orphan \"$cmdline\"; then\n-    log \"skip live or unproven daemon pid=$pid\"\n-  if [ \"$REAP_DAEMONS\" = \"1\" ]; then\n-      log \"skip changed daemon pid=$pid\"\n-      *node*context-server.js*) ;;\n-        log \"skip changed daemon pid=$pid\"\n-    if ! _daemon_cmdline_is_orphan \"$current_cmdline\"; then\n-      log \"skip live daemon pid=$pid\"\n-  ORPHANS=$((ORPHANS+1))\n=== commit dates ===\na69a621a39 2026-08-21 feat(sk-git): make the worktree base directory configurable\nf83952c3a9 2026-09-11 fix(sk-git): keep the reaper off live sessions and record autosync rewrites\n3c7c3f8387 2026-09-03 refactor(runtime): remove the memory launcher, plugin, hooks and the tool-ownership commit gate\n=== README invariant ===\n| `bash .skilled/bin/skilled-loop [claude|pi|opencode|codex|cursor|hermes|devin] [args...]` | CLI wrapper | Run one of seven runtimes under one loop id (`cursor` launches `cursor-agent`). The wrapper relaunches eligible sessions with a handoff seed. Claude, Pi, OpenCode, Codex and Hermes arm automatically through their adapters. Cursor and Devin never arm. They enter through `/speckit:handoff`. When the session exits with the record still pending, the wrapper prints the manual claim command. Each relaunch it starts is recorded in the hop history that `session-relaunch.cjs history` prints. |\n| `source /path/to/repo/.skilled/bin/skilled-loop-shell.sh` | Shell shim | Defines `claude`, `pi`, `opencode`, `codex`, `hermes`, `devin` and `cursor-agent` as functions that start an interactive session through the nearest `.skilled/bin/skilled-loop` at or above the current directory, a symlinked `.skilled` included. Subcommands, print and one-shot modes, version and help, non-terminal launches and sessions already under a loop run the binary directly. `skilled_loop_resolve <runtime> [args...]` prints the wrapper the shim would use, or nothing. |\n| `node .skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs` | CLI | Start the system-skill-advisor daemon. |\n| `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs <tool> [flags]` | CLI | Call any of the 9 system-skill-advisor tools from a shell. pass `--trusted` for maintainer mutations. |\n| `node .skilled/bin/hf-model-server.cjs` | CLI | Start the local embedding server (via `main`). |\n| `createHfModelServer` | Function | Build an embedding server instance with `listen`, `close`, `dispose` and `inject` for tests. |\n| `assertLoopbackBindAllowed` | Function | Refuse non-loopback binds unless remote bind plus auth token are set. |\n| `bash .skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh <runtime> [args]` | CLI | Launch an AI session in its own git worktree + branch + isolated MCP databases. Top-level sessions isolate. orchestrated children (`AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` or already inside a linked worktree) exec in place. `--dry-run` prints the plan. |\n| `bash .skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh [--dry-run]` | CLI | Prune merged + clean per-session worktrees, stale socket dirs and session markers. never signals a process. Auto-reap is restricted to proven-inactive exact `work/<runtime>/<slug>` pairs (the whole marker file must match a PID grammar, a malformed marker is treated as ambiguous and the worktree is kept. the branch's runtime/slug must equal the directory basename). |\n| `bash .skilled/bin/worktree-guard.sh` | CLI / SessionStart hook | Detect-and-warn: prints a one-line stderr warning when a top-level session is on shared `main`/`master` instead of an isolated worktree. Non-fatal (always exits 0). silent for children, inside worktrees, non-git dirs, or with `SPECKIT_WORKTREE_GUARD=off`. |\n| `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub <id> --prompt \"<task>\"` | CLI | Ask whether the compiled router is authoritative for a hub. Returns a legacy sentinel when it is not. `--prompt-stdin` reads the prompt from stdin instead, which keeps a user's prompt out of the process table. `--surface-hint <SURFACE>` passes the surface the caller's session works in. A specific surface hint leads a keyword tie between surfaces the prompt matched. A hint naming the fallback surface (SKILLED for sk-code) changes nothing, because the fallback always ranks last. |\n| `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-status.cjs --all` | CLI | Report per-hub serving authority and a cause code separating expected drift from breakage. |\n| `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-guard.cjs [--warn-only] [--json]` | CLI | Fail when a hub's serving manifest no longer matches its inputs, when the runtime and its authored source disagree, or when the authored manifest is missing. Each failure names the manifest to copy or restore. |\n| `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-sync.cjs [--check] [--verify] [--finalize <path>] [--revert <path>]` | CLI | Trace the authored closure, publish it atomically, and finalize or revert the retained rollback. The build and `--check` stop with one line naming the folder to restore when the authored source is missing. |\n| `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-manifest.cjs <command>` | CLI | Mint, refresh or inspect a hub activation manifest through the library in `lib/`. |\n| `node .skilled/bin/check-no-spec-imports.cjs` | CLI | Prove no file here reaches into the spec tree at runtime. |\n=== daemon start times ===\n1157 Sun Oct 11 18:29:55 2026\n5979 Tue Oct 27 10:45:09 2026\n35266 Sat Oct 24 15:47:29 2026\n36974 Sun Oct 18 19:30:42 2026\n47838 Thu Oct 22 06:19:20 2026\n55634 Wed Oct 14 09:17:55 2026\n76538 Fri Oct 23 17:42:16 2026\n83785 Mon Oct 19 08:37:59 2026\n90965 Tue Oct 27 09:25:47 2026\n91756 Fri Oct 23 22:15:10 2026\n95634 Tue Oct 27 08:56:30 2026\n99077 Tue Oct 27 08:55:08 2026\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== deletion diff (daemon-related) ===\n-# Prune finished per-session AI worktrees, report orphan daemons.\n-# Companion to worktree-session.sh. Keeps .worktrees/ and the MCP daemon population\n-#   - REPORT (does not kill) MCP daemons whose recorded lease points at a .worktrees/ dir\n-#   --reap-daemons   Also SIGTERM (then SIGKILL) daemons whose worktree DB dir is gone.\n-#                    Off by default — daemon killing is opt-in to protect live sessions.\n-# checkout. Never kills a daemon whose worktree still exists.\n-REAP_DAEMONS=0\n-    --reap-daemons) REAP_DAEMONS=1 ;;\n-# Extract the worktree path a daemon cmdline points at, but only when it sits\n-_daemon_worktree_path_from_cmdline() {\n-_daemon_cmdline_is_orphan() {\n-  if ! worktree_path=\"$(_daemon_worktree_path_from_cmdline \"$cmdline\")\"; then\n-# 5. ORPHAN DAEMON REPORTING\n-# --- orphan daemon reporting (kill only with --reap-daemons) ---------------\n-# A worktree daemon writes its lease under <worktree-db-dir>/.system-spec-memory-launcher.json.\n-# If that lease names a live childPid but the worktree DB dir is gone, it is orphaned.\n-log \"scanning for orphan worktree daemons\"\n-ORPHANS=0\n-# is gone, so we instead detect live daemon PIDs whose cwd/db-dir no longer resolves.\n-# Conservative heuristic: list node daemons referencing a .worktrees/ path that is absent.\n-    *node*context-server.js*) ;;\n-  if ! _daemon_cmdline_is_orphan \"$cmdline\"; then\n-    log \"skip live or unproven daemon pid=$pid\"\n-  if [ \"$REAP_DAEMONS\" = \"1\" ]; then\n-      log \"skip changed daemon pid=$pid\"\n-      *node*context-server.js*) ;;\n-        log \"skip changed daemon pid=$pid\"\n-    if ! _daemon_cmdline_is_orphan \"$current_cmdline\"; then\n-      log \"skip live daemon pid=$pid\"\n-  ORPHANS=$((ORPHANS+1))\n=== commit dates ===\na69a621a39 2026-08-21 feat(sk-git): make the worktree base directory configurable\nf83952c3a9 2026-09-11 fix(sk-git): keep the reaper off live sessions and record autosync rewrites\n3c7c3f8387 2026-09-03 refactor(runtime): remove the memory launcher, plugin, hooks and the tool-ownership commit gate\n=== README invariant ===\n| `bash .skilled/bin/skilled-loop [claude|pi|opencode|codex|cursor|hermes|devin] [args...]` | CLI wrapper | Run one of seven runtimes under one loop id (`cursor` launches `cursor-agent`). The wrapper relaunches eligible sessions with a handoff seed. Claude, Pi, OpenCode, Codex and Hermes arm automatically through their adapters. Cursor and Devin never arm. They enter through `/speckit:handoff`. When the session exits with the record still pending, the wrapper prints the manual claim command. Each relaunch it starts is recorded in the hop history that `session-relaunch.cjs history` prints. |\n| `source /path/to/repo/.skilled/bin/skilled-loop-shell.sh` | Shell shim | Defines `claude`, `pi`, `opencode`, `codex`, `hermes`, `devin` and `cursor-agent` as functions that start an interactive session through the nearest `.skilled/bin/skilled-loop` at or above the current directory, a symlinked `.skilled` included. Subcommands, print and one-shot modes, version and help, non-terminal launches and sessions already under a loop run the binary directly. `skilled_loop_resolve <runtime> [args...]` prints the wrapper the shim would use, or nothing. |\n| `node .skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs` | CLI | Start the system-skill-advisor daemon. |\n| `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs <tool> [flags]` | CLI | Call any of the 9 system-skill-advisor tools from a shell. pass `--trusted` for maintainer mutations. |\n| `node .skilled/bin/hf-model-server.cjs` | CLI | Start the local embedding server (via `main`). |\n| `createHfModelServer` | Function | Build an embedding server instance with `listen`, `close`, `dispose` and `inject` for tests. |\n| `assertLoopbackBindAllowed` | Function | Refuse non-loopback binds unless remote bind plus auth token are set. |\n| `bash .skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh <runtime> [args]` | CLI | Launch an AI session in its own git worktree + branch + isolated MCP databases. Top-level sessions isolate. orchestrated children (`AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` or already inside a linked worktree) exec in place. `--dry-run` prints the plan. |\n| `bash .skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh [--dry-run]` | CLI | Prune merged + clean per-session worktrees, stale socket dirs and session markers. never signals a process. Auto-reap is restricted to proven-inactive exact `work/<runtime>/<slug>` pairs (the whole marker file must match a PID grammar, a malformed marker is treated as ambiguous and the worktree is kept. the branch's runtime/slug must equal the directory basename). |\n| `bash .skilled/bin/worktree-guard.sh` | CLI / SessionStart hook | Detect-and-warn: prints a one-line stderr warning when a top-level session is on shared `main`/`master` instead of an isolated worktree. Non-fatal (always exits 0). silent for children, inside worktrees, non-git dirs, or with `SPECKIT_WORKTREE_GUARD=off`. |\n| `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub <id> --prompt \"<task>\"` | CLI | Ask whether the compiled router is authoritative for a hub. Returns a legacy sentinel when it is not. `--prompt-stdin` reads the prompt from stdin instead, which keeps a user's prompt out of the process table. `--surface-hint <SURFACE>` passes the surface the caller's session works in. A specific surface hint leads a keyword tie between surfaces the prompt matched. A hint naming the fallback surface (SKILLED for sk-code) changes nothing, because the fallback always ranks last. |\n| `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-status.cjs --all` | CLI | Report per-hub serving authority and a cause code separating expected drift from breakage. |\n| `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-guard.cjs [--warn-only] [--json]` | CLI | Fail when a hub's serving manifest no longer matches its inputs, when the runtime and its authored source disagree, or when the authored manifest is missing. Each failure names the manifest to copy or restore. |\n| `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-sync.cjs [--check] [--verify] [--finalize <path>] [--revert <path>]` | CLI | Trace the authored closure, publish it atomically, and finalize or revert the retained rollback. The build and `--check` stop with one line naming the folder to restore when the authored source is missing. |\n| `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route-manifest.cjs <command>` | CLI | Mint, refresh or inspect a hub activation manifest through the library in `lib/`. |\n| `node .skilled/bin/check-no-spec-imports.cjs` | CLI | Prove no file here reaches into the spec tree at runtime. |\n=== daemon start times ===\n1157 Sun Oct 11 18:29:55 2026\n5979 Tue Oct 27 10:45:09 2026\n35266 Sat Oct 24 15:47:29 2026\n36974 Sun Oct 18 19:30:42 2026\n47838 Thu Oct 22 06:19:20 2026\n55634 Wed Oct 14 09:17:55 2026\n76538 Fri Oct 23 17:42:16 2026\n83785 Mon Oct 19 08:37:59 2026\n90965 Tue Oct 27 09:25:47 2026\n91756 Fri Oct 23 22:15:10 2026\n95634 Tue Oct 27 08:56:30 2026\n99077 Tue Oct 27 08:55:08 2026\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public && echo \\\"=== deletion diff (daemon-related) ===\\\" && git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh | grep -E \\\"^[-+].*(daemon|DAEMON|orphan|ORPHAN|context-server)\\\" | head -30; echo \\\"=== commit dates ===\\\" && git log -1 --format=\\\"%h %ad %s\\\" --date=short a69a621a39a && git log -1 --format=\\\"%h %ad %s\\\" --date=short f83952c3a94 && git log -1 --format=\\\"%h %ad %s\\\" --date=short 3c7c3f83874; echo \\\"=== README invariant ===\\\" && sed -n '160,175p' .skilled/bin/README.md; echo \\\"=== daemon start times ===\\\" && ps -Ao pid,lstart,command | grep \\\"[f]smonitor--daemon run\\\" |