{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793094838892,"sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","part":{"partID":"prt_17cc7e50a001rxf0g5dzuGHjue","sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","messageID":"msg_17cc7aeb6001pPalNvatcsXQtC","type":"tool","id":"call_c7e175f4c8154bf545df7453","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public && echo \"=== reaper token count ===\" && grep -c -i -E \"daemon|fsmonitor|orphan\" .skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh; echo \"=== naming default ===\" && sed -n '65,80p' .skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh; echo \"=== changelog ===\" && grep -n -i \"worktrees\\|worktreeBase\" .skilled/skills/sk-git/changelog/v1.5.2.0.md | head -8; echo \"=== move commit ===\" && git log -1 --format=\"%h %ad %s\" --date=short 330427cf308; echo \"=== gitignore ===\" && grep -n \"worktrees\" .gitignore | head -3"},"output":"=== reaper token count ===\n0\n=== naming default ===\n_wn_base_dir() {\n  local top raw\n  top=\"$(_wn_toplevel)\" || return 1\n  raw=\"${SPECKIT_WORKTREE_BASE:-$(git -C \"$top\" config --get speckit.worktreeBase 2>/dev/null || true)}\"\n  [ -n \"$raw\" ] || raw=\".worktrees\"\n  case \"$raw\" in\n    \"~\")   raw=\"$HOME\" ;;\n    \"~/\"*) raw=\"$HOME/${raw#\\~/}\" ;;\n  esac\n  case \"$raw\" in\n    /*) printf '%s\\n' \"$raw\" ;;\n    *)  printf '%s\\n' \"$top/$raw\" ;;\n  esac\n}\n\n# Per-namespace high-water files keep the two counters independent.\n=== changelog ===\n3:description: \"This release makes the worktree base configurable so worktrees can live outside the primary checkout.\"\n8:  - \"worktrees outside primary checkout\"\n13:This release makes the worktree base configurable so worktrees can live outside the primary checkout.\n17:Nesting dozens of worktrees under `.worktrees/` forces tools that scan from the repo root, including `git status`, the fsmonitor daemon, Git GUIs and file-sync clients, to walk every worktree's `node_modules` on each pass. On large trees, that shows up as sustained CPU.\n21:- **The worktree base is configurable.** Set `SPECKIT_WORKTREE_BASE` or `speckit.worktreeBase` to choose where worktrees live. The environment value takes precedence over git config. The default is still in-checkout `.worktrees`, relative to the main toplevel, so other clones, CI and the test suite are unaffected unless a base is explicitly configured.\n23:- **Validation accepts worktrees from either base.** `is_valid_pair` validates a `worktrees/NNN-slug` branch against a directory whose basename is `NNN-slug` under the configured base or the legacy `.worktrees` parent, so worktrees from before and after relocation both pass.\n24:- **Session launch and cleanup use the same base.** `worktree-session.sh` places session worktrees there, while `worktree-reaper.sh` prunes and daemon-orphan-detects against it. The reaper's orphan detection now anchors on the resolved base by canonicalizing each candidate path's parent rather than matching a fixed `.worktrees/` string, which also makes it immune to `/var` versus `/private/var` symlink skew.\n25:- **Relocation preserves numbering and safety rules.** Number allocation scans each registered worktree's basename regardless of location, so moving the base cannot reissue a live number. Branch grammar (`worktrees/NNN-slug`, `branches/NNN-slug`), the locked per-namespace allocator, remote-push permission and every pre-push/commit gate are unchanged.\n=== move commit ===\n330427cf30 2026-09-17 refactor(source-root): move the authored asset tree from .opencode to .skilled\n=== gitignore ===\n320:.worktrees/\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== reaper token count ===\n0\n=== naming default ===\n_wn_base_dir() {\n  local top raw\n  top=\"$(_wn_toplevel)\" || return 1\n  raw=\"${SPECKIT_WORKTREE_BASE:-$(git -C \"$top\" config --get speckit.worktreeBase 2>/dev/null || true)}\"\n  [ -n \"$raw\" ] || raw=\".worktrees\"\n  case \"$raw\" in\n    \"~\")   raw=\"$HOME\" ;;\n    \"~/\"*) raw=\"$HOME/${raw#\\~/}\" ;;\n  esac\n  case \"$raw\" in\n    /*) printf '%s\\n' \"$raw\" ;;\n    *)  printf '%s\\n' \"$top/$raw\" ;;\n  esac\n}\n\n# Per-namespace high-water files keep the two counters independent.\n=== changelog ===\n3:description: \"This release makes the worktree base configurable so worktrees can live outside the primary checkout.\"\n8:  - \"worktrees outside primary checkout\"\n13:This release makes the worktree base configurable so worktrees can live outside the primary checkout.\n17:Nesting dozens of worktrees under `.worktrees/` forces tools that scan from the repo root, including `git status`, the fsmonitor daemon, Git GUIs and file-sync clients, to walk every worktree's `node_modules` on each pass. On large trees, that shows up as sustained CPU.\n21:- **The worktree base is configurable.** Set `SPECKIT_WORKTREE_BASE` or `speckit.worktreeBase` to choose where worktrees live. The environment value takes precedence over git config. The default is still in-checkout `.worktrees`, relative to the main toplevel, so other clones, CI and the test suite are unaffected unless a base is explicitly configured.\n23:- **Validation accepts worktrees from either base.** `is_valid_pair` validates a `worktrees/NNN-slug` branch against a directory whose basename is `NNN-slug` under the configured base or the legacy `.worktrees` parent, so worktrees from before and after relocation both pass.\n24:- **Session launch and cleanup use the same base.** `worktree-session.sh` places session worktrees there, while `worktree-reaper.sh` prunes and daemon-orphan-detects against it. The reaper's orphan detection now anchors on the resolved base by canonicalizing each candidate path's parent rather than matching a fixed `.worktrees/` string, which also makes it immune to `/var` versus `/private/var` symlink skew.\n25:- **Relocation preserves numbering and safety rules.** Number allocation scans each registered worktree's basename regardless of location, so moving the base cannot reissue a live number. Branch grammar (`worktrees/NNN-slug`, `branches/NNN-slug`), the locked per-namespace allocator, remote-push permission and every pre-push/commit gate are unchanged.\n=== move commit ===\n330427cf30 2026-09-17 refactor(source-root): move the authored asset tree from .opencode to .skilled\n=== gitignore ===\n320:.worktrees/\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public && echo \\\"=== reaper token count ===\\\" && grep -c -i -E \\\"daemon|fsmonitor|orphan\\\" .skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh; echo \\\"=== naming default ===\\\" && sed -n '65,80p' .skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh; echo \\\"=== changelog ===\\\" && grep -n -i \\\"worktrees\\\\|worktreeBase\\\" .skilled/skills/sk-git/changelog/v1.5.2.0.md | head -8; echo \\\"=== move commit ===\\\" && git log -1 --format=\\\"%h %ad %s\\\" --date=short 330427cf308; echo \\\"=== gitignore ===\\\" && grep -n \\\"worktrees\\\" .gitignore | head -3\"}"},"time":{"start":1793094837514,"end":1793094838892}}}}
