{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793094906454,"sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","part":{"partID":"prt_17cc881d0001bwKpDB9jK4hzO1","sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","messageID":"msg_17cc87a8f001qoBfTcV4gFiPLp","type":"tool","id":"call_d92f26b019fba77a382416a9","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 1: The sk-git/026 regression — who moved the worktrees back and where the reaper's daemon handling went\n\n## Focus\n\nQ1 of the packet's section 8: what unset `speckit.worktreeBase` and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and whether anything still defaults worktrees to `.worktrees/`. This iteration reads the completed sk-git/026 packet, the current worktree scripts, and the git history of the reaper and the base write-back, then re-measures the live worktree and daemon population.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Read `specs/sk-git/026-worktree-hygiene-and-relocation/implementation-summary.md` for the recorded outcomes (prune, fsmonitor on, configurable base set to `~/worktrees/public`, reaper \"generalized daemon-orphan detection\").\n2. Read the resolved-base code paths: `.skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh` `_wn_base_dir()`, `.skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh` base resolution and config write-back, and the current `.skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh`.\n3. Traced the reaper's history with `git log --oneline -S \"daemon\"` over both the pre-move `.opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh` and the current `.skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh`, then read the daemon-related diff hunks of the commit that dropped the block.\n4. Traced the config write-back history with `git log --oneline -S 'config speckit.worktreeBase \"$WT_BASE_DIR\"'` over both path spellings.\n5. Re-measured the live state: `git config --show-origin --get-regexp 'fsmonitor|untracked|worktreeBase|extensions'`, `ls -d .worktrees/*`, `ls ~/worktrees`, and a `ps -Ao pid,lstart,command` census of `fsmonitor--daemon run` processes.\n6. Checked the reaper's published invariant in `.skilled/bin/README.md` and the v1.5.2.0 changelog entry for the documented default.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. The reaper's daemon handling was deleted by `3c7c3f83874` (2026-09-03, \"refactor(runtime): remove the memory launcher, plugin, hooks and the tool-ownership commit gate\"), not by the `.opencode` → `.skilled` source-root move (`330427cf30`, 2026-09-17). The diff removes `--reap-daemons`, `_daemon_worktree_path_from_cmdline()`, `_daemon_cmdline_is_orphan()`, and the whole \"5. ORPHAN DAEMON REPORTING\" block. [SOURCE: git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh]\n2. The deleted logic only matched `pgrep -f 'context-server\\.js'` and skipped any command line not matching `*node*context-server.js*` — the retired spec-memory MCP daemons, never `git fsmonitor--daemon`. The packet's premise conflates two daemon families. [SOURCE: git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh]\n3. Restoring \"the reaper's daemon handling\" would not stop a single fsmonitor daemon; a fsmonitor reaper is new work, not a revert. [INFERENCE: from findings 1-2 plus `grep -c -i -E \"daemon|fsmonitor|orphan\" .skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh` returning 0]\n4. The current reaper's published invariant is \"never signals a process\" (`.skilled/bin/README.md`), so re-adding daemon killing inside `worktree-reaper.sh` would break a documented contract rather than restore one. [SOURCE: .skilled/bin/README.md:168]\n5. `speckit.worktreeBase` is local-only configuration: `git config --show-origin --get-regexp` prints only `file:.git/config core.fsmonitor true` and `core.untrackedcache true`, and no commit can unset an unversioned `.git/config` key. The relocation policy record simply is not in the repository. [SOURCE: git config --show-origin --get-regexp output, this session]\n6. The durable in-checkout default is re-created by the launch wrapper itself. `.skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:293-294` writes `speckit.worktreeBase = $WT_BASE_DIR` whenever the key is unset, and lines 219-227 resolve `SPECKIT_WORKTREE_BASE` → config → default `.worktrees`, absolutized to `$MAIN_ROOT/.worktrees`. One launch without the env var converts the intended `~/worktrees/public` policy into a permanent in-checkout policy. [SOURCE: .skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:219] [SOURCE: .skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:293]\n7. The auto-pin is recent: `f83952c3a94` (2026-09-11, \"fix(sk-git): keep the reaper off live sessions and record autosync rewrites\") introduced the config write-back, three weeks after `a69a621a39a` (2026-08-21) introduced the configurable base. The window between the two commits is exactly when a launch could have re-pinned `.worktrees` without operator intent. [SOURCE: git log -S 'config speckit.worktreeBase \"$WT_BASE_DIR\"' -- .opencode/bin/worktree-session.sh .skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh]\n8. `.worktrees` remains the documented code default: `_wn_base_dir()` falls back to `.worktrees` relative to the toplevel when neither env nor config names a base, and the v1.5.2.0 changelog states \"The default is still in-checkout `.worktrees`\". `.worktrees/` is gitignored (`.gitignore:320`) but sits inside the checkout, so the main daemon watches it. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh:69] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-git/changelog/v1.5.2.0.md:21] [SOURCE: .gitignore:320]\n9. The live state matches the in-checkout default: `~/worktrees` is empty and 13 worktrees sit under `Public/.worktrees/`. The empty relocated base is the residue of the relocation, not of a live policy. [SOURCE: ls -d .worktrees/*, this session] [SOURCE: ls ~/worktrees, this session]\n10. Twelve `git fsmonitor--daemon run --detach --ipc-threads=8` processes are alive as of 09:54Z, the oldest started Oct 11 18:29:55 (PID 1157, 16 days), and four started today alone (08:55, 08:56, 09:25, 10:45) — the population is still growing during this research session. Nothing in the repo starts, stops, or bounds them. [SOURCE: ps -Ao pid,lstart,command output, this session]\n\n## Questions Answered\n\n- Q1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default? — Answer: two different events. The reaper's daemon block was deleted by `3c7c3f83874` (2026-09-03) in the memory-launcher refactor, and it only ever targeted MCP `context-server.js` daemons. The base key was not unset by any commit (it is unversioned local config); the launch wrapper re-pins it on any unset launch, defaulting to `.worktrees`. Yes — `.worktrees` remains the code default, 13 worktrees live there, and 12 fsmonitor daemons persist from Oct 11 onward.\n\n## Questions Remaining\n\n- Q2. Git 2.50.1's documented daemon lifecycle on macOS (idle exit, `fsmonitor.socketDir`, `git fsmonitor--daemon stop` on a wedged daemon).\n- Q3. Event overload versus a known 2.50.1 daemon deadlock (`--ipc-threads`, cookie handshake).\n- Q4. Which hook/script git call sites lack a timeout.\n- Q5. Safest default shape.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- \"The `.opencode` → `.skilled` move removed the daemon handling.\" Ruled out: `git log -S daemon` puts the deletion in `3c7c3f83874` (2026-09-03), and the move commit `330427cf30` (2026-09-17) is the only commit touching the current path.\n- \"A repo commit reverted the relocated worktree base.\" Ruled out: the key is local config; the only repo-side actor is the wrapper's write-back.\n- \"The relocation never happened or was rolled back by hand.\" Ruled out: the sk-git/026 summary records the migration and the file-count drop; `~/worktrees` exists but is empty, which is the relocation's residue.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Git-config provenance for `speckit.worktreeBase`: `.git/config` is not versioned, so the exact unset action is unrecoverable from the repository. Recorded as an explicit UNKNOWN rather than guessed.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Contradictory evidence: the packet's own wording calls the removed code \"the reaper's daemon handling\" and the current pile-up \"fsmonitor daemons\", which reads as one lineage of work. The code shows two unrelated daemon families. Resolution: recorded as findings 1-3 rather than smoothed over; the premise correction is load-bearing for the fix design.\n- Missing dependency: no access to the pre-unset `.git/config`; the UNKNOWN stands with the check that would resolve it (a `.git/config` copy in a backup or another clone's config).\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `specs/sk-git/026-worktree-hygiene-and-relocation/implementation-summary.md`\n- `git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh`\n- `git log --oneline -S \"daemon\" -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh .skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh`\n- `git log --oneline -S 'config speckit.worktreeBase \"$WT_BASE_DIR\"' -- .opencode/bin/worktree-session.sh .skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh`\n- `git log -1 --format=\"%h %ad %s\" --date=short a69a621a39a f83952c3a94 3c7c3f83874 330427cf308`\n- `.skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:219-229,293-294`\n- `.skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh`\n- `.skilled/bin/README.md:168`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh:65-79`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-git/changelog/v1.5.2.0.md:21-24`\n- `.gitignore:320`\n- `ps -Ao pid,lstart,command | grep [f]smonitor--daemon run` (12 processes)\n- `git config --show-origin --get-regexp \"fsmonitor|untracked|worktreeBase|extensions\"`\n- `ls -d .worktrees/*`, `ls ~/worktrees`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.85\n- Questions addressed: Q1\n- Questions answered: Q1\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: `git log -S` over both path spellings, then reading the daemon-related diff hunks of the one commit that matched, converted a vague \"the reaper lost something\" into an exact deletion with a date and a reason. Re-measuring the live process census in the same session kept the sixteen-day-old daemon observation current instead of inherited.\n- What did not work and why: chasing config provenance through git history was structurally impossible — the key is unversioned. Reading the wrapper's write-back found the real persistence mechanism instead.\n- What I would do differently: start from the code path that writes the key (write-back) rather than from \"who unset it\", because an unset that is silently re-pinned is a different bug from an unset that stays unset.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nQ2 and Q3 together: git 2.50.1's fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS — whether a daemon can exit on its own, what `fsmonitor.socketDir`, idle shutdown and `git fsmonitor--daemon stop` do, and whether `--ipc-threads=8` or the cookie handshake has a known wedge in this version. The `--ipc-threads=8` argument in every live process is not something this repo passes, so its origin and its deadlock surface need an authoritative answer.\n","path":"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-undated-run2/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-undated-run2/iterations/iteration-001.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-undated-run2/iterations/iteration-001.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 1: The sk-git/026 regression — who moved the worktrees back and where the reaper's daemon handling went\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nQ1 of the packet's section 8: what unset `speckit.worktreeBase` and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and whether anything still defaults worktrees to `.worktrees/`. This iteration reads the completed sk-git/026 packet, the current worktree scripts, and the git history of the reaper and the base write-back, then re-measures the live worktree and daemon population.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Read `specs/sk-git/026-worktree-hygiene-and-relocation/implementation-summary.md` for the recorded outcomes (prune, fsmonitor on, configurable base set to `~/worktrees/public`, reaper \\\"generalized daemon-orphan detection\\\").\\n2. Read the resolved-base code paths: `.skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh` `_wn_base_dir()`, `.skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh` base resolution and config write-back, and the current `.skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh`.\\n3. Traced the reaper's history with `git log --oneline -S \\\"daemon\\\"` over both the pre-move `.opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh` and the current `.skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh`, then read the daemon-related diff hunks of the commit that dropped the block.\\n4. Traced the config write-back history with `git log --oneline -S 'config speckit.worktreeBase \\\"$WT_BASE_DIR\\\"'` over both path spellings.\\n5. Re-measured the live state: `git config --show-origin --get-regexp 'fsmonitor|untracked|worktreeBase|extensions'`, `ls -d .worktrees/*`, `ls ~/worktrees`, and a `ps -Ao pid,lstart,command` census of `fsmonitor--daemon run` processes.\\n6. Checked the reaper's published invariant in `.skilled/bin/README.md` and the v1.5.2.0 changelog entry for the documented default.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. The reaper's daemon handling was deleted by `3c7c3f83874` (2026-09-03, \\\"refactor(runtime): remove the memory launcher, plugin, hooks and the tool-ownership commit gate\\\"), not by the `.opencode` → `.skilled` source-root move (`330427cf30`, 2026-09-17). The diff removes `--reap-daemons`, `_daemon_worktree_path_from_cmdline()`, `_daemon_cmdline_is_orphan()`, and the whole \\\"5. ORPHAN DAEMON REPORTING\\\" block. [SOURCE: git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh]\\n2. The deleted logic only matched `pgrep -f 'context-server\\\\.js'` and skipped any command line not matching `*node*context-server.js*` — the retired spec-memory MCP daemons, never `git fsmonitor--daemon`. The packet's premise conflates two daemon families. [SOURCE: git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh]\\n3. Restoring \\\"the reaper's daemon handling\\\" would not stop a single fsmonitor daemon; a fsmonitor reaper is new work, not a revert. [INFERENCE: from findings 1-2 plus `grep -c -i -E \\\"daemon|fsmonitor|orphan\\\" .skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh` returning 0]\\n4. The current reaper's published invariant is \\\"never signals a process\\\" (`.skilled/bin/README.md`), so re-adding daemon killing inside `worktree-reaper.sh` would break a documented contract rather than restore one. [SOURCE: .skilled/bin/README.md:168]\\n5. `speckit.worktreeBase` is local-only configuration: `git config --show-origin --get-regexp` prints only `file:.git/config core.fsmonitor true` and `core.untrackedcache true`, and no commit can unset an unversioned `.git/config` key. The relocation policy record simply is not in the repository. [SOURCE: git config --show-origin --get-regexp output, this session]\\n6. The durable in-checkout default is re-created by the launch wrapper itself. `.skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:293-294` writes `speckit.worktreeBase = $WT_BASE_DIR` whenever the key is unset, and lines 219-227 resolve `SPECKIT_WORKTREE_BASE` → config → default `.worktrees`, absolutized to `$MAIN_ROOT/.worktrees`. One launch without the env var converts the intended `~/worktrees/public` policy into a permanent in-checkout policy. [SOURCE: .skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:219] [SOURCE: .skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:293]\\n7. The auto-pin is recent: `f83952c3a94` (2026-09-11, \\\"fix(sk-git): keep the reaper off live sessions and record autosync rewrites\\\") introduced the config write-back, three weeks after `a69a621a39a` (2026-08-21) introduced the configurable base. The window between the two commits is exactly when a launch could have re-pinned `.worktrees` without operator intent. [SOURCE: git log -S 'config speckit.worktreeBase \\\"$WT_BASE_DIR\\\"' -- .opencode/bin/worktree-session.sh .skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh]\\n8. `.worktrees` remains the documented code default: `_wn_base_dir()` falls back to `.worktrees` relative to the toplevel when neither env nor config names a base, and the v1.5.2.0 changelog states \\\"The default is still in-checkout `.worktrees`\\\". `.worktrees/` is gitignored (`.gitignore:320`) but sits inside the checkout, so the main daemon watches it. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh:69] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/sk-git/changelog/v1.5.2.0.md:21] [SOURCE: .gitignore:320]\\n9. The live state matches the in-checkout default: `~/worktrees` is empty and 13 worktrees sit under `Public/.worktrees/`. The empty relocated base is the residue of the relocation, not of a live policy. [SOURCE: ls -d .worktrees/*, this session] [SOURCE: ls ~/worktrees, this session]\\n10. Twelve `git fsmonitor--daemon run --detach --ipc-threads=8` processes are alive as of 09:54Z, the oldest started Oct 11 18:29:55 (PID 1157, 16 days), and four started today alone (08:55, 08:56, 09:25, 10:45) — the population is still growing during this research session. Nothing in the repo starts, stops, or bounds them. [SOURCE: ps -Ao pid,lstart,command output, this session]\\n\\n## Questions Answered\\n\\n- Q1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default? — Answer: two different events. The reaper's daemon block was deleted by `3c7c3f83874` (2026-09-03) in the memory-launcher refactor, and it only ever targeted MCP `context-server.js` daemons. The base key was not unset by any commit (it is unversioned local config); the launch wrapper re-pins it on any unset launch, defaulting to `.worktrees`. Yes — `.worktrees` remains the code default, 13 worktrees live there, and 12 fsmonitor daemons persist from Oct 11 onward.\\n\\n## Questions Remaining\\n\\n- Q2. Git 2.50.1's documented daemon lifecycle on macOS (idle exit, `fsmonitor.socketDir`, `git fsmonitor--daemon stop` on a wedged daemon).\\n- Q3. Event overload versus a known 2.50.1 daemon deadlock (`--ipc-threads`, cookie handshake).\\n- Q4. Which hook/script git call sites lack a timeout.\\n- Q5. Safest default shape.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- \\\"The `.opencode` → `.skilled` move removed the daemon handling.\\\" Ruled out: `git log -S daemon` puts the deletion in `3c7c3f83874` (2026-09-03), and the move commit `330427cf30` (2026-09-17) is the only commit touching the current path.\\n- \\\"A repo commit reverted the relocated worktree base.\\\" Ruled out: the key is local config; the only repo-side actor is the wrapper's write-back.\\n- \\\"The relocation never happened or was rolled back by hand.\\\" Ruled out: the sk-git/026 summary records the migration and the file-count drop; `~/worktrees` exists but is empty, which is the relocation's residue.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Git-config provenance for `speckit.worktreeBase`: `.git/config` is not versioned, so the exact unset action is unrecoverable from the repository. Recorded as an explicit UNKNOWN rather than guessed.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Contradictory evidence: the packet's own wording calls the removed code \\\"the reaper's daemon handling\\\" and the current pile-up \\\"fsmonitor daemons\\\", which reads as one lineage of work. The code shows two unrelated daemon families. Resolution: recorded as findings 1-3 rather than smoothed over; the premise correction is load-bearing for the fix design.\\n- Missing dependency: no access to the pre-unset `.git/config`; the UNKNOWN stands with the check that would resolve it (a `.git/config` copy in a backup or another clone's config).\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `specs/sk-git/026-worktree-hygiene-and-relocation/implementation-summary.md`\\n- `git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh`\\n- `git log --oneline -S \\\"daemon\\\" -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh .skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh`\\n- `git log --oneline -S 'config speckit.worktreeBase \\\"$WT_BASE_DIR\\\"' -- .opencode/bin/worktree-session.sh .skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh`\\n- `git log -1 --format=\\\"%h %ad %s\\\" --date=short a69a621a39a f83952c3a94 3c7c3f83874 330427cf308`\\n- `.skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:219-229,293-294`\\n- `.skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh`\\n- `.skilled/bin/README.md:168`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh:65-79`\\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-git/changelog/v1.5.2.0.md:21-24`\\n- `.gitignore:320`\\n- `ps -Ao pid,lstart,command | grep [f]smonitor--daemon run` (12 processes)\\n- `git config --show-origin --get-regexp \\\"fsmonitor|untracked|worktreeBase|extensions\\\"`\\n- `ls -d .worktrees/*`, `ls ~/worktrees`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.85\\n- Questions addressed: Q1\\n- Questions answered: Q1\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: `git log -S` over both path spellings, then reading the daemon-related diff hunks of the one commit that matched, converted a vague \\\"the reaper lost something\\\" into an exact deletion with a date and a reason. Re-measuring the live process census in the same session kept the sixteen-day-old daemon observation current instead of inherited.\\n- What did not work and why: chasing config provenance through git history was structurally impossible — the key is unversioned. Reading the wrapper's write-back found the real persistence mechanism instead.\\n- What I would do differently: start from the code path that writes the key (write-back) rather than from \\\"who unset it\\\", because an unset that is silently re-pinned is a different bug from an unset that stays unset.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nQ2 and Q3 together: git 2.50.1's fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS — whether a daemon can exit on its own, what `fsmonitor.socketDir`, idle shutdown and `git fsmonitor--daemon stop` do, and whether `--ipc-threads=8` or the cookie handshake has a known wedge in this version. The `--ipc-threads=8` argument in every live process is not something this repo passes, so its origin and its deadlock surface need an authoritative answer.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-undated-run2/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793094877648,"end":1793094906454}}}}
