{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793094933406,"sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","part":{"partID":"prt_17cc91bab001MBiis96vFHB0qV","sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","messageID":"msg_17cc8f76a001HiHD8OiPV6calm","type":"tool","id":"call_b4f968dd9a89eb0f28027e56","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":1,\"run\":1,\"runId\":\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-undated-run2-1793094321851-ufzori\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-undated-run2-1793094321851-ufzori\",\"lineageId\":\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-undated-run2-1793094321851-ufzori\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"newInfoRatio\":0.85,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"The sk-git/026 regression: who moved the worktrees back and where the reaper's daemon handling went\",\"findingsCount\":10,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Seven of ten findings are new to the packet: the deletion commit identity, the MCP-versus-fsmonitor family correction, the wrapper config write-back and its commit, the documented default, and the refreshed census were all unrecorded.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Q1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default?\",\"Q2. What is git 2.50.1's documented fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS, and how do fsmonitor.socketDir, idle shutdown and git fsmonitor--daemon stop behave when the daemon is wedged?\",\"Q3. Is event overload the real cause of the hang, or is there a known daemon deadlock in this git version, for example around --ipc-threads or the cookie-file handshake?\",\"Q4. Which call sites in the repo's hooks and scripts run git without a timeout, and which of them should opt out of fsmonitor?\",\"Q5. What is the safest default: fsmonitor on with worktrees outside the checkout, or fsmonitor off for the main checkout and on per worktree?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"Q1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"The .opencode to .skilled move removed the daemon handling\",\"A repo commit reverted the relocated worktree base\",\"The relocation never happened or was rolled back by hand\"],\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Bash\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\"specs/sk-git/026-worktree-hygiene-and-relocation/implementation-summary.md\",\"git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\",\"git log -S daemon -- .skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\",\"git log -S config speckit.worktreeBase -- .opencode/bin/worktree-session.sh .skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh\",\".skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:219\",\".skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:293\",\".skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\",\".skilled/bin/README.md:168\",\".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh:69\",\".skilled/skills/sk-git/changelog/v1.5.2.0.md:21\",\".gitignore:320\",\"ps -Ao pid,lstart,command\",\"git config --show-origin --get-regexp\",\".worktrees/\",\"~/worktrees\"],\"edgeCase\":\"contradictory-evidence\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-27T09:54:34Z\",\"durationMs\":0,\"graphEvents\":[{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"q1-base-and-reaper\",\"kind\":\"QUESTION\",\"label\":\"What unset the worktree base and removed the reaper daemon handling\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-reaper-deleted-by-memory-refactor\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Reaper daemon block deleted by commit 3c7c3f83874\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-mcp-vs-fsmonitor\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Removed logic targeted MCP context-server daemons, never git fsmonitor\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-wrapper-repins-base\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Launch wrapper writes speckit.worktreeBase back on every unset launch\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-daemon-census-12\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Twelve fsmonitor daemons alive, oldest 16 days\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q1-1\",\"source\":\"f-reaper-deleted-by-memory-refactor\",\"target\":\"q1-base-and-reaper\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q1-2\",\"source\":\"f-mcp-vs-fsmonitor\",\"target\":\"f-reaper-deleted-by-memory-refactor\",\"relation\":\"CONTRADICTS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q1-3\",\"source\":\"f-wrapper-repins-base\",\"target\":\"q1-base-and-reaper\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q1-4\",\"source\":\"f-daemon-census-12\",\"target\":\"q1-base-and-reaper\",\"relation\":\"SUPPORTS\"}]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-001\",\"label\":\"Commit 3c7c3f83874 (2026-09-03) deleted the reaper's --reap-daemons flag, the _daemon_worktree_path_from_cmdline and _daemon_cmdline_is_orphan helpers, and the whole ORPHAN DAEMON REPORTING block from .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-002\",\"label\":\"The deleted reaper logic only enumerated pgrep -f context-server.js and skipped any command line not matching *node*context-server.js*, so it targeted retired spec-memory MCP daemons and never matched git fsmonitor--daemon.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"git show 3c7c3f83874 -- .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-003\",\"label\":\"Restoring the reaper's daemon handling would not stop a single fsmonitor daemon; a fsmonitor reaper is new work rather than a revert.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\",\".skilled/skills/sk-git/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-004\",\"label\":\"The current reaper's published invariant is never signals a process, so re-adding daemon killing inside worktree-reaper.sh would break a documented contract rather than restore one.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/bin/README.md:168\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-005\",\"label\":\"speckit.worktreeBase is unversioned local config: no commit can unset it, and this checkout currently has no such key set, so the relocation policy record simply is not in the repository.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"git config --show-origin --get-regexp fsmonitor|untracked|worktreeBase|extensions\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-006\",\"label\":\".skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:293-294 writes speckit.worktreeBase whenever the key is unset, and lines 219-227 default to <toplevel>/.worktrees, so one launch without SPECKIT_WORKTREE_BASE re-pins the in-checkout base permanently.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:219\",\".skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:293\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-007\",\"label\":\"The auto-pin arrived in f83952c3a94 (2026-09-11), three weeks after a69a621a39a (2026-08-21) made the base configurable; the window between the two commits is when a launch could have re-pinned .worktrees without operator intent.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"git log -S config speckit.worktreeBase -- .opencode/bin/worktree-session.sh .skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-008\",\"label\":\".worktrees remains the documented code default: _wn_base_dir() falls back to .worktrees relative to the toplevel, the v1.5.2.0 changelog states the default is still in-checkout, and .worktrees/ is gitignored but inside the checkout so the main daemon watches it.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/worktree-naming.sh:69\",\".skilled/skills/sk-git/changelog/v1.5.2.0.md:21\",\".gitignore:320\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-009\",\"label\":\"The live state matches the in-checkout default: ~/worktrees is empty and 13 worktrees sit under Public/.worktrees/; the empty relocated base is the residue of the relocation, not of a live policy.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"ls -d .worktrees/*, this session\",\"ls ~/worktrees, this session\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-010\",\"label\":\"Twelve fsmonitor--daemon run --detach --ipc-threads=8 processes are alive as of 09:54Z, oldest PID 1157 from Oct 11 18:29:55 (16 days), four started today alone; nothing in the repo starts, stops, or bounds them.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"ps -Ao pid,lstart,command output, this session\"]}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"The .opencode to .skilled move removed the daemon handling\",\"reason\":\"git log -S daemon puts the deletion in 3c7c3f83874 (2026-09-03); the move commit 330427cf30 (2026-09-17) is the only commit touching the current path.\",\"iteration\":1}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"A repo commit reverted the relocated worktree base\",\"reason\":\"The key is unversioned local config; the only repo-side actor is the wrapper's write-back.\",\"iteration\":1}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"The relocation never happened or was rolled back by hand\",\"reason\":\"The sk-git/026 summary records the migration and the file-count drop; ~/worktrees exists but is empty, which is the relocation's residue.\",\"iteration\":1}\n","path":"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-undated-run2/deltas/iter-001.jsonl"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-undated-run2/deltas/iter-001.jsonl","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-undated-run2/deltas/iter-001.jsonl"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"{\\\"type\\\":\\\"iteration\\\",\\\"