{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793095000867,"sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","part":{"partID":"prt_17cca5366001vqx2UyKC622s45","sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","messageID":"msg_17cca3b71001kl0yq69KINglsO","type":"tool","id":"call_6c97555d300bb8cddc6cfac2","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"echo \"=== daemon lines 190-215 ===\"; curl -s --max-time 30 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/v2.50.1/builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c | sed -n '190,215p'; echo \"=== ipcthreads default ===\"; curl -s --max-time 30 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/v2.50.1/builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c | grep -n -B2 -A6 \"ipcthreads\" | head -40; echo \"=== starttimeout default ===\"; curl -s --max-time 30 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/v2.50.1/builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c | grep -n -B2 -A6 \"starttimeout\" | head -30; echo \"=== relnotes fsmonitor 2.51/2.52/2.53 ===\"; for v in 2.51.0 2.52.0 2.53.0; do echo \"-- $v --\"; curl -s --max-time 30 \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/v$v/Documentation/RelNotes/$v.adoc\" | grep -c -i fsmonitor; done"},"output":"=== daemon lines 190-215 ===\n\t/*\n\t * Technically, close() and unlink() can fail, but we don't\n\t * care here.  We only created the file to trigger a watch\n\t * event from the FS to know that when we're up to date.\n\t */\n\tclose(fd);\n\tunlink(cookie_pathname.buf);\n\n\t/*\n\t * Technically, this is an infinite wait (well, unless another\n\t * thread sends us an abort).  I'd like to change this to\n\t * use `pthread_cond_timedwait()` and return an error/timeout\n\t * and let the caller do the trivial response thing, but we\n\t * don't have that routine in our thread-utils.\n\t *\n\t * After extensive beta testing I'm not really worried about\n\t * this.  Also note that the above open() and unlink() calls\n\t * will cause at least two FS events on that path, so the odds\n\t * of getting stuck are pretty slim.\n\t */\n\twhile (cookie->result == FCIR_INIT)\n\t\tpthread_cond_wait(&state->cookies_cond,\n\t\t\t\t  &state->main_lock);\n\ndone:\n\thashmap_remove(&state->cookies, &cookie->entry, NULL);\n=== ipcthreads default ===\n33- * Global state loaded from config.\n34- */\n35:#define FSMONITOR__IPC_THREADS \"fsmonitor.ipcthreads\"\n36-static int fsmonitor__ipc_threads = 8;\n37-\n38-#define FSMONITOR__START_TIMEOUT \"fsmonitor.starttimeout\"\n39-static int fsmonitor__start_timeout_sec = 60;\n40-\n41-#define FSMONITOR__ANNOUNCE_STARTUP \"fsmonitor.announcestartup\"\n=== starttimeout default ===\n36-static int fsmonitor__ipc_threads = 8;\n37-\n38:#define FSMONITOR__START_TIMEOUT \"fsmonitor.starttimeout\"\n39-static int fsmonitor__start_timeout_sec = 60;\n40-\n41-#define FSMONITOR__ANNOUNCE_STARTUP \"fsmonitor.announcestartup\"\n42-static int fsmonitor__announce_startup = 0;\n43-\n44-static int fsmonitor_config(const char *var, const char *value,\n=== relnotes fsmonitor 2.51/2.52/2.53 ===\n-- 2.51.0 --\n0\n-- 2.52.0 --\n0\n-- 2.53.0 --\n0\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":1},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== daemon lines 190-215 ===\n\t/*\n\t * Technically, close() and unlink() can fail, but we don't\n\t * care here.  We only created the file to trigger a watch\n\t * event from the FS to know that when we're up to date.\n\t */\n\tclose(fd);\n\tunlink(cookie_pathname.buf);\n\n\t/*\n\t * Technically, this is an infinite wait (well, unless another\n\t * thread sends us an abort).  I'd like to change this to\n\t * use `pthread_cond_timedwait()` and return an error/timeout\n\t * and let the caller do the trivial response thing, but we\n\t * don't have that routine in our thread-utils.\n\t *\n\t * After extensive beta testing I'm not really worried about\n\t * this.  Also note that the above open() and unlink() calls\n\t * will cause at least two FS events on that path, so the odds\n\t * of getting stuck are pretty slim.\n\t */\n\twhile (cookie->result == FCIR_INIT)\n\t\tpthread_cond_wait(&state->cookies_cond,\n\t\t\t\t  &state->main_lock);\n\ndone:\n\thashmap_remove(&state->cookies, &cookie->entry, NULL);\n=== ipcthreads default ===\n33- * Global state loaded from config.\n34- */\n35:#define FSMONITOR__IPC_THREADS \"fsmonitor.ipcthreads\"\n36-static int fsmonitor__ipc_threads = 8;\n37-\n38-#define FSMONITOR__START_TIMEOUT \"fsmonitor.starttimeout\"\n39-static int fsmonitor__start_timeout_sec = 60;\n40-\n41-#define FSMONITOR__ANNOUNCE_STARTUP \"fsmonitor.announcestartup\"\n=== starttimeout default ===\n36-static int fsmonitor__ipc_threads = 8;\n37-\n38:#define FSMONITOR__START_TIMEOUT \"fsmonitor.starttimeout\"\n39-static int fsmonitor__start_timeout_sec = 60;\n40-\n41-#define FSMONITOR__ANNOUNCE_STARTUP \"fsmonitor.announcestartup\"\n42-static int fsmonitor__announce_startup = 0;\n43-\n44-static int fsmonitor_config(const char *var, const char *value,\n=== relnotes fsmonitor 2.51/2.52/2.53 ===\n-- 2.51.0 --\n0\n-- 2.52.0 --\n0\n-- 2.53.0 --\n0\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Exited with code 1"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"echo \\\"=== daemon lines 190-215 ===\\\"; curl -s --max-time 30 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/v2.50.1/builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c | sed -n '190,215p'; echo \\\"=== ipcthreads default ===\\\"; curl -s --max-time 30 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/v2.50.1/builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c | grep -n -B2 -A6 \\\"ipcthreads\\\" | head -40; echo \\\"=== starttimeout default ===\\\"; curl -s --max-time 30 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/v2.50.1/builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c | grep -n -B2 -A6 \\\"starttimeout\\\" | head -30; echo \\\"=== relnotes fsmonitor 2.51/2.52/2.53 ===\\\"; for v in 2.51.0 2.52.0 2.53.0; do echo \\\"-- $v --\\\"; curl -s --max-time 30 \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/v$v/Documentation/RelNotes/$v.adoc\\\" | grep -c -i fsmonitor; done\"}"},"time":{"start":1793094996838,"end":1793095000867}}}}
