{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793095091748,"sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","part":{"partID":"prt_17ccb83bf001EG6O29Sk03sELU","sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","messageID":"msg_17ccb6709001faL6HMLPQqW6OM","type":"tool","id":"call_b1fe180eba97f7586b310035","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":2,\"run\":2,\"runId\":\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-undated-run2-1793094321851-ufzori\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-undated-run2-1793094321851-ufzori\",\"lineageId\":\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-undated-run2-1793094321851-ufzori\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"newInfoRatio\":0.9,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Git 2.50.1 daemon lifecycle and the wedge: an acknowledged infinite wait, not a repo bug\",\"findingsCount\":10,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Nine of ten findings are new to the packet: the unbounded cookie wait with its source comment, the client read with no deadline, the empty Darwin health stub, the stop polling loop, the compiled ipcthreads default, and the empty 2.51-2.53 release notes were all unrecorded.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Q1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default?\",\"Q2. What is git 2.50.1's documented fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS, and how do fsmonitor.socketDir, idle shutdown and git fsmonitor--daemon stop behave when the daemon is wedged?\",\"Q3. Is event overload the real cause of the hang, or is there a known daemon deadlock in this git version, for example around --ipc-threads or the cookie-file handshake?\",\"Q4. Which call sites in the repo's hooks and scripts run git without a timeout, and which of them should opt out of fsmonitor?\",\"Q5. What is the safest default: fsmonitor on with worktrees outside the checkout, or fsmonitor off for the main checkout and on per worktree?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"Q2. What is git 2.50.1's documented fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS, and how do fsmonitor.socketDir, idle shutdown and git fsmonitor--daemon stop behave when the daemon is wedged?\",\"Q3. Is event overload the real cause of the hang, or is there a known daemon deadlock in this git version, for example around --ipc-threads or the cookie-file handshake?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"--ipc-threads=8 is a repo or Apple-specific tuning knob that might itself deadlock\",\"A git upgrade fixes it\",\"The daemon can be expected to exit on its own after idling\"],\"toolsUsed\":[\"Bash\",\"WebFetch\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\"man git-fsmonitor--daemon\",\"builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c (git v2.50.1):35-42,84-101,190-215\",\"compat/simple-ipc/ipc-unix-socket.c (git v2.50.1):195-217\",\"compat/fsmonitor/fsm-health-darwin.c (git v2.50.1)\",\"compat/fsmonitor/fsm-health.h (git v2.50.1)\",\"Documentation/RelNotes/2.51.0.adoc\",\"Documentation/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc\",\"Documentation/RelNotes/2.53.0.adoc\",\"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/scratch/findings.md\"],\"edgeCase\":\"contradictory-evidence\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-27T09:57:21Z\",\"durationMs\":0,\"graphEvents\":[{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"q2-daemon-lifecycle\",\"kind\":\"QUESTION\",\"label\":\"Does the daemon ever exit on its own and how does stop behave when wedged\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"q3-overload-vs-deadlock\",\"kind\":\"QUESTION\",\"label\":\"Is the hang event overload or a known deadlock\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-infinite-wait-cookie\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Cookie handshake wait is an acknowledged infinite wait in the source\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-client-read-no-deadline\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"IPC client response read has no poll and no deadline\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-darwin-health-stub\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"macOS health thread is an empty stub, so no self-exit\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-stop-polls-forever\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"git fsmonitor--daemon stop polls forever on a wedged daemon\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-ipcthreads-compiled-default\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"--ipc-threads=8 is git's compiled default, not repo config\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-no-upgrade-fix\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"No fsmonitor fix announced in 2.51-2.53 release notes\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q2-1\",\"source\":\"f-darwin-health-stub\",\"target\":\"q2-daemon-lifecycle\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q2-2\",\"source\":\"f-stop-polls-forever\",\"target\":\"q2-daemon-lifecycle\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q3-1\",\"source\":\"f-infinite-wait-cookie\",\"target\":\"q3-overload-vs-deadlock\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q3-2\",\"source\":\"f-client-read-no-deadline\",\"target\":\"q3-overload-vs-deadlock\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q3-3\",\"source\":\"f-ipcthreads-compiled-default\",\"target\":\"q3-overload-vs-deadlock\",\"relation\":\"CONTRADICTS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q3-4\",\"source\":\"f-no-upgrade-fix\",\"target\":\"q3-overload-vs-deadlock\",\"relation\":\"SUPPORTS\"}]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter002-001\",\"label\":\"The manual documents the daemon only as a long running process with start/run/stop/status; no idle timeout, no lifetime bound, no self-exit condition.\",\"iteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"man git-fsmonitor--daemon (Git 2.50.1)\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter002-002\",\"label\":\"fsmonitor.socketDir only relocates the Unix socket when .git or $HOME is on a network-mounted filesystem; it has no lifecycle effect on a native-filesystem checkout.\",\"iteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"man git-fsmonitor--daemon (Git 2.50.1)\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter002-003\",\"label\":\"On macOS the health thread is an empty stub (ctor/loop/stop_async all return immediately) while the header contract says it should call ipc_server_stop_async to cause shutdown, so the daemon never monitors itself and never exits on health grounds.\",\"iteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"compat/fsmonitor/fsm-health-darwin.c:8-27\",\"compat/fsmonitor/fsm-health.h:31-45\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter002-004\",\"label\":\"git fsmonitor--daemon stop sends quit then polls fsmonitor_ipc__get_state() every 50 ms with no deadline, so on a daemon that cannot answer the stop command hangs, matching the packet's observed 15-second kill.\",\"iteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c:84-101\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter002-005\",\"label\":\"fsmonitor.starttimeout (60 s default) is the only timeout in the lifecycle and bounds startup alone; fsmonitor.ipcthreads (8 default) sizes the worker pool; neither bounds a running query.\",\"iteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c:35-39\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter002-006\",\"label\":\"Daemon side: every non-quit query creates a cookie file in the watched tree and blocks in pthread_cond_wait until the event thread reports the cookie seen; the source comment states this is an infinite wait and that pthread_cond_timedwait was unavailable in their thread-utils.\",\"iteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c:198-212\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter002-007\",\"label\":\"Client side: ipc_client_send_command_to_connection writes the command then calls read_packetized_to_strbuf with no poll and no deadline; only EOF or a read error unblocks it, and the error string on that path is exactly the could not read IPC response the packet observed from git fetch.\",\"iteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"compat/simple-ipc/ipc-unix-socket.c:210-213\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter002-008\",\"label\":\"--ipc-threads=8 is git's compiled default (static int fsmonitor__ipc_threads = 8), not repo or Apple configuration; this checkout sets no fsmonitor.* key. It multiplies parked clients but is not the cause.\",\"iteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c:36\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter002-009\",\"label\":\"No announced fix exists: release notes for 2.51.0, 2.52.0 and 2.53.0 contain zero fsmonitor entries; upgrading is not the fix path.\",\"iteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"Documentation/RelNotes/2.51.0.adoc\",\"Documentation/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc\",\"Documentation/RelNotes/2.53.0.adoc\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter002-010\",\"label\":\"The trigger is a lost cookie event: the source notes the cookie's open/unlink cause at least two FS events and the odds of getting stuck are slim, but a daemon watching roughly 2.5M files can drop one under load; one undelivered event parks one worker forever and eight parked clients saturate the pool so status and stop stop answering.\",\"iteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c:206-212\",\"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/scratch/findings.md\"]}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"--ipc-threads=8 is a repo or Apple-specific tuning knob that might itself deadlock\",\"reason\":\"8 is the compiled default of fsmonitor.ipcthreads and the repo sets no fsmonitor.* key; it remains a risk multiplier, not a root cause.\",\"iteration\":2}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"A git upgrade fixes it\",\"reason\":\"Release notes for 2.51-2.53 contain zero fsmonitor entries; the 2.50.1 source states the timed wait was not implemented.\",\"iteration\":2}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"The daemon can be expected to exit on its own after idling\",\"reason\":\"No idle timeout exists in the manual or the source, and the macOS health thread is an empty stub.\",\"iteration\":2}\n","path":"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-undated-run2/deltas/iter-002.jsonl"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-undated-run2/deltas/iter-002.jsonl","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-undated-run2/deltas/iter-002.jsonl"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"{\\\"type\\\":\\\"iteration\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":2,\\\"run\\\":2,\\\"runId\\\":\\\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-undated-run2-1793094321851-ufzori\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-undated-run2-1793094321851-ufzori\\\",\\\"lineageId\\\":\\\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-undated-run2-1793094321851-ufzori\\\",\\\"mode\\\":\\\"research\\\",\\\"target_agent\\\":\\\"deep-research\\\",\\\"agent_definition_loaded\\\":true,\\\"resolved_route\\\":\\\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\\\",\\\"newInfoRatio\\\":0.9,\\\"status\\\":\\\"complete\\\",\\\"focus\\\":\\\"Git 2.50.1 daemon lifecycle and the wedge: an acknowledged infinite wait, not a repo bug\\\",\\\"findingsCount\\\":10,\\\"noveltyJustification\\\":\\\"Nine of ten findings are new to the packet: the unbounded cookie wait with its source comment, the client read with no deadline, the empty Darwin health stub, the stop polling loop, the compiled ipcthreads default, and the empty 2.51-2.53 release notes were all unrecorded.\\\",\\\"keyQuestions\\\":[\\\"Q1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default?\\\",\\\"Q2. What is git 2.50.1's documented fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS, and how do fsmonitor.socketDir, idle shutdown and git fsmonitor--daemon stop behave when the daemon is wedged?\\\",\\\"Q3. Is event overload the real cause of the hang, or is there a known daemon deadlock in this git version, for example around --ipc-threads or the cookie-file handshake?\\\",\\\"Q4. Which call sites in the repo's hooks and scripts run git without a timeout, and which of them should opt out of fsmonitor?\\\",\\\"Q5. What is the safest default: fsmonitor on with worktrees outside the checkout, or fsmonitor off for the main checkout and on per worktree?\\\"],\\\"answeredQuestions\\\":[\\\"Q2. What is git 2.50.1's documented fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS, and how do fsmonitor.socketDir, idle shutdown and git fsmonitor--daemon stop behave when the daemon is wedged?\\\",\\\"Q3. Is event overload the real cause of the hang, or is there a known daemon deadlock in this git version, for example around --ipc-threads or the cookie-file handshake?\\\"],\\\"ruledOut\\\":[\\\"--ipc-threads=8 is a repo or Apple-specific tuning knob that might itself deadlock\\\",\\\"A git upgrade fixes it\\\",\\\"The daemon can be expected to exit on its own after idling\\\"],\\\"toolsUsed\\\":[\\\"Bash\\\",\\\"WebFetch\\\"],\\\"sourcesQueried\\\":[\\\"man git-fsmonitor--daemon\\\",\\\"builtin/fsmonitor--daemon.c (git v2.50.1):35-42,84-101,190-215\\\",\\\"compat/simple-ipc/ipc-unix-socket.c (git v2.50.1):195-217\\\",\\\"compat/fsmonitor/fsm-health-darwin.c (git v2.50.1)\\\",\\\"compat/fsmonitor/fsm-health.h (git v2.50.1)\\\",\\\"Documentation/RelNotes/2.51.0.adoc\\\",\\\"Documentation/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc\\\",\\\"Documentation/RelNotes/2.53.0.adoc\\\",\\\"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/scratch/findings.md\\\"],\\\"edgeCase\\\":\\\"contradictory-evidence\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-10-27T09:57:21Z\\\",\\\"durationMs\\\":0,\\\"graphEvents\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"q2-daemon-lifecycle\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"QUESTION\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Does the daemon ever exit on its own and how does stop behave when wedged\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"q3-overload-vs-deadlock\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"QUESTION\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Is the hang event overload or a known deadlock\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-infinite-wait-cookie\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Cookie handshake wait is an acknowledged infinite wait in the source\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-client-read-no-deadline\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"IPC client response read has no poll and no deadline\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-darwin-health-stub\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"macOS health thread is an empty stub, so no self-exit\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-stop-polls-forever\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"git fsmonitor--daemon stop polls forever on a wedged daemon\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-ipcthreads-compiled-default\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"--ipc-threads=8 is git's compiled default, not repo config\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-no-upgrade-fix\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"No fsmonitor fix announced in 2.51-2.53 release notes\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"edge\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"e-q2-1\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"f-darwin-health-stub\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"q2-daemon-lifecycle\\\",\\\"relation\\\":\\\"ANSWERS\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"edge\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"e-q2-2\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"f-stop-polls-forever\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"q2-daemon-lifecycle\\\",\\\"relation\\\":\\\"ANSWERS\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"edge\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"e-q3-1\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"f-infinite-wait-cookie\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"q3-overload-vs-deadlock\\\",\\\"relation\\\":\\\"ANSWERS\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"edge\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"e-q3-2\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"f-client-read-no-deadline\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"q3-overload-vs-deadlock\\\",\\\"relation\\\":\\\"ANSWERS\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"edge\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"e-q3-3\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"f-ipcthreads-compiled-default\\\",\\\"t