{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793095101403,"sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","part":{"partID":"prt_17ccbe60f002WzJXVP18IEkO3U","sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","messageID":"msg_17ccbcc63001VUJkthqQ6RZAf9","type":"tool","id":"call_96e2c4a6b05baca7542a849d","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"L=\"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-undated-run2\"; node -e '\nconst fs=require(\"fs\");\nconst raw=fs.readFileSync(process.argv[1],\"utf8\");\nconst lines=raw.split(/\\r?\\n/).filter(Boolean);\nlet bad=0;\nlines.forEach((l,i)=>{try{JSON.parse(l)}catch(e){bad++;console.log(\"BAD line\",i+1,e.message)}});\nconsole.log(\"lines:\",lines.length,\"bad:\",bad);\n' \"$L/deltas/iter-002.jsonl\"; grep -n \"manifest\" \"$L/iterations/iteration-002.md\""},"output":"lines: 14 bad: 0\n76:Q4 and Q5 together: inventory every git call site in the repo's hooks and scripts that can block on the fsmonitor IPC (with `generate-leaf-manifest.cjs:129` as the proven one), decide which need a timeout versus `-c core.fsmonitor=false`, and turn the lifecycle facts into a default posture plus a daemon-reaping design that does not contradict the reaper's \"never signals a process\" invariant.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"lines: 14 bad: 0\n76:Q4 and Q5 together: inventory every git call site in the repo's hooks and scripts that can block on the fsmonitor IPC (with `generate-leaf-manifest.cjs:129` as the proven one), decide which need a timeout versus `-c core.fsmonitor=false`, and turn the lifecycle facts into a default posture plus a daemon-reaping design that does not contradict the reaper's \"never signals a process\" invariant.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"L=\\\"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-