{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793095228240,"sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","part":{"id":"prt_17ccddb50001T8Ciy2cwur0q1u","sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","messageID":"msg_17ccdd0a6001BI6DqffmGnhfAh","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793095252814,"sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","part":{"partID":"prt_17ccddb54002ZvneXeNFYmq38V","sessionID":"ses_e833fbb1effewOnhN31WYdpXxT","messageID":"msg_17ccdd0a6001BI6DqffmGnhfAh","type":"tool","id":"call_48c64b44ffade7ad2ef0b99d","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":3,\"run\":3,\"runId\":\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-undated-run2-1793094321851-ufzori\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-undated-run2-1793094321851-ufzori\",\"lineageId\":\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-undated-run2-1793094321851-ufzori\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"newInfoRatio\":0.9,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"The repo's unbounded git call sites and the safest default posture\",\"findingsCount\":10,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Nine of ten findings are new to the packet: the hook chain to the hung spawnSync, the existing GIT_NO_FSMONITOR convention, the sibling unbounded call sites, the timeout precedents, the socket attribution, and the derived default posture were all unrecorded.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"Q1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default?\",\"Q2. What is git 2.50.1's documented fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS, and how do fsmonitor.socketDir, idle shutdown and git fsmonitor--daemon stop behave when the daemon is wedged?\",\"Q3. Is event overload the real cause of the hang, or is there a known daemon deadlock in this git version, for example around --ipc-threads or the cookie-file handshake?\",\"Q4. Which call sites in the repo's hooks and scripts run git without a timeout, and which of them should opt out of fsmonitor?\",\"Q5. What is the safest default: fsmonitor on with worktrees outside the checkout, or fsmonitor off for the main checkout and on per worktree?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"Q4. Which call sites in the repo's hooks and scripts run git without a timeout, and which of them should opt out of fsmonitor?\",\"Q5. What is the safest default: fsmonitor on with worktrees outside the checkout, or fsmonitor off for the main checkout and on per worktree?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Disable fsmonitor everywhere\",\"Match daemons by command line\",\"Rely on git fsmonitor--daemon stop in a reaper\",\"Restore the reaper's daemon handling\"],\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Bash\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/generate-leaf-manifest.cjs:129\",\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs:51\",\"~/.config/git/hooks/pre-push:417\",\".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/scripts/verify-router-sync.cjs:168\",\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/regenerate-skill-derived.cjs:73\",\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-source-tags-helper.mjs:206\",\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/shared/scripts/cite-drift-scan.mjs:145\",\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/validation/continuity-freshness.ts:38\",\".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/scripts/lib/run-check.cjs:28\",\".skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.sh:20\",\".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/lib/message-contract.mjs:262\",\".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-message-gate.mjs:290\",\"rg git spawn sites under .skilled\",\"lsof socket attribution PIDs 1157,5979\"],\"edgeCase\":\"partial-success\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-27T09:59:59Z\",\"durationMs\":0,\"graphEvents\":[{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"q4-call-sites\",\"kind\":\"QUESTION\",\"label\":\"Which git call sites lack a timeout and which should opt out of fsmonitor\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"q5-safest-default\",\"kind\":\"QUESTION\",\"label\":\"Safest default posture for fsmonitor and worktrees\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-hung-site-no-ceiling\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"generate-leaf-manifest.cjs:129 has no timeout and no fsmonitor opt-out\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-hook-chain\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Pre-push gate chain reaches the hung spawnSync via ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-git-no-fsmonitor-convention\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Repo already uses -c core.fsmonitor=false in six or more call sites\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-sibling-unbounded-sites\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"verify-router-sync and regenerate-skill-derived check-ignore calls are unbounded\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-timeout-precedents\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"GIT_TIMEOUT_MS and timeout:3000 are existing repo patterns\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-socket-attribution\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Main daemon identifiable by .git/fsmonitor--daemon.ipc socket path\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-default-posture\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Safest default: fsmonitor on with worktrees outside the checkout\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q4-1\",\"source\":\"f-hung-site-no-ceiling\",\"target\":\"q4-call-sites\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q4-2\",\"source\":\"f-hook-chain\",\"target\":\"f-hung-site-no-ceiling\",\"relation\":\"SUPPORTS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q4-3\",\"source\":\"f-git-no-fsmonitor-convention\",\"target\":\"q4-call-sites\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q4-4\",\"source\":\"f-sibling-unbounded-sites\",\"target\":\"q4-call-sites\",\"relation\":\"SUPPORTS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q4-5\",\"source\":\"f-timeout-precedents\",\"target\":\"q4-call-sites\",\"relation\":\"SUPPORTS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q5-1\",\"source\":\"f-default-posture\",\"target\":\"q5-safest-default\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-q5-2\",\"source\":\"f-socket-attribution\",\"target\":\"q5-safest-default\",\"relation\":\"SUPPORTS\"}]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter003-001\",\"label\":\"The proven hung site has no ceiling and no opt-out: generate-leaf-manifest.cjs:129-133 runs spawnSync git check-ignore with no timeout option and no -c core.fsmonitor=false, and the fallback at line 136 only handles a returned failure, so a hang is never rescued.\",\"iteration\":3,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/generate-leaf-manifest.cjs:129\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter003-002\",\"label\":\"The pre-push hook runs ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs which imports buildManifestBytes from the manifest builder; the hook's own comment says the gate finishes in about a second, which is the assumption that failed.\",\"iteration\":3,\"sources\":[\"~/.config/git/hooks/pre-push:417\",\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs:51\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter003-003\",\"label\":\"The repository already has the fix convention: GIT_NO_FSMONITOR = ['-c','core.fsmonitor=false'] appears in cite-drift-scan.mjs, continuity-freshness.ts, check-source-tags-helper.mjs and run-check.cjs, plus git -c core.fsmonitor=false in hook-flags.sh and the QC playbook; adopting it at the hung site is the low-risk change.\",\"iteration\":3,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/shared/scripts/cite-drift-scan.mjs:145\",\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/validation/continuity-freshness.ts:38\",\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-source-tags-helper.mjs:53\",\".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/scripts/lib/run-check.cjs:28\",\".skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.sh:20\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter003-004\",\"label\":\"Other unbounded fsmonitor-touching call sites: verify-router-sync.cjs:168 and regenerate-skill-derived.cjs:73 run check-ignore with no opt-out and no timeout; generate-leaf-manifest.cjs:111 (rev-parse) and check-source-tags-helper.mjs:206 (opt-out present) also lack timeouts.\",\"iteration\":3,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/scripts/verify-router-sync.cjs:168\",\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/regenerate-skill-derived.cjs:73\",\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-source-tags-helper.mjs:206\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter003-005\",\"label\":\"The repo does use timeouts elsewhere: message-contract.mjs wraps every git call in GIT_TIMEOUT_MS and git-message-gate.mjs uses timeout: 3000 for rev-parse, so the fix is a choice between two existing conventions.\",\"iteration\":3,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/lib/message-contract.mjs:262\",\".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-message-gate.mjs:290\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter003-006\",\"label\":\"Roughly 59 files under .skilled spawn git; the highest-risk class is index-reading commands (check-ignore, status, ls-files) against the main checkout because those query the fsmonitor daemon; non-index commands (rev-parse, log, show, cat-file) never touch it.\",\"iteration\":3,\"sources\":[\"rg spawnSync/execSync/execFileSync git under .skilled (59 files)\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter003-007\",\"label\":\"Live attribution: the main-checkout daemon holds /Users/.../Public/.git/fsmonitor--daemon.ipc (PID 5979, started 10:45:09) while worktree daemons hold a fsmonitor--daemon.ipc under their per-worktree git dirs; the socket path is the attribution key because every daemon's argv is identical.\",\"iteration\":3,\"sources\":[\"lsof output, this session\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter003-008\",\"label\":\"A fsmonitor reaper cannot use git fsmonitor--daemon stop as its escalation path because stop polls forever on exactly the wedged daemon a reaper must remove; reaping means signalling the PID directly, which contradicts the current reaper's never-signals-a-process invariant, so a fsmonitor reap belongs in a separate entry point with its own stated invariant.\",\"iteration\":3,\"sources\":[\".skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\",\".skilled/bin/README.md:168\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter003-009\",\"label\":\"Q5: the safest default is fsmonitor on with worktrees outside the checkout; it removes the trigger (the main daemon's event volume from ~2M worktree files) rather than masking it and keeps the benefit on the 570k-file main checkout, while the per-worktree opt-out requires extensions.worktreeConfig (absent today), loses the largest benefit and leaves worktree daemons free to wedge their own commands.\",\"iteration\":3,\"sources\":[\"git config --show-origin --get-regexp, this session\",\"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/scratch/findings.md\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter003-010\",\"label\":\"Durability requires two changes together: set speckit.worktreeBase explicitly and stop the write-back from persisting the default as policy, otherwise the next launch without SPECKIT_WORKTREE_BASE re-pins .worktrees and the relocation silently reverts; under every option the hook ceiling is required because a wedge can still occur in any worktree.\",\"iteration\":3,\"sources\":[\".skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:293\"]}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"Disable fsmonitor everywhere\",\"reason\":\"Rejected as the default rather than ruled out as an option: it discards a measured benefit on a 570k-file checkout, and per-worktree config gives the same safety with a narrower blast radius.\",\"iteration\":3}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"Match daemons by command line\",\"reason\":\"All daemons share identical argv; the socket path is the only attribution key.\",\"iteration\":3}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"Rely on git fsmonitor--daemon stop in a reaper\",\"reason\":\"stop polls forever on a wedged daemon, so it cannot be the escalation path by itself.\",\"iteration\":3}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"Restore the reaper's daemon handling\",\"reason\":\"The deleted code targeted MCP context-server daemons and the current reaper promises never to signal a process.\",\"iteration\":3}\n","path":"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-undated-run2/deltas/iter-003.jsonl"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-undated-run2/deltas/iter-003.jsonl","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-undated-run2/deltas/iter-003.jsonl"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"{\\\"type\\\":\\\"iteration\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"run\\\":3,\\\"runId\\\":\\\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-undated-run2-1793094321851-ufzori\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-undated-run2-1793094321851-ufzori\\\",\\\"lineageId\\\":\\\"fanout-llmgateway-flash-undated-run2-1793094321851-ufzori\\\",\\\"mode\\\":\\\"research\\\",\\\"target_agent\\\":\\\"deep-research\\\",\\\"agent_definition_loaded\\\":true,\\\"resolved_route\\\":\\\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\\\",\\\"newInfoRatio\\\":0.9,\\\"status\\\":\\\"complete\\\",\\\"focus\\\":\\\"The repo's unbounded git call sites and the safest default posture\\\",\\\"findingsCount\\\":10,\\\"noveltyJustification\\\":\\\"Nine of ten findings are new to the packet: the hook chain to the hung spawnSync, the existing GIT_NO_FSMONITOR convention, the sibling unbounded call sites, the timeout precedents, the socket attribution, and the derived default posture were all unrecorded.\\\",\\\"keyQuestions\\\":[\\\"Q1. What unset speckit.worktreeBase and removed the reaper's daemon handling, and does anything still create worktrees under .worktrees/ by default?\\\",\\\"Q2. What is git 2.50.1's documented fsmonitor daemon lifecycle on macOS, and how do fsmonitor.socketDir, idle shutdown and git fsmonitor--daemon stop behave when the daemon is wedged?\\\",\\\"Q3. Is event overload the real cause of the hang, or is there a known daemon deadlock in this git version, for example around --ipc-threads or the cookie-file handshake?\\\",\\\"Q4. Which call sites in the repo's hooks and scripts run git without a timeout, and which of them should opt out of fsmonitor?\\\",\\\"Q5. What is the safest default: fsmonitor on with worktrees outside the checkout, or fsmonitor off for the main checkout and on per worktree?\\\"],\\\"answeredQuestions\\\":[\\\"Q4. Which call sites in the repo's hooks and scripts run git without a timeout, and which of them should opt out of fsmonitor?\\\",\\\"Q5. What is the safest default: fsmonitor on with worktrees outside the checkout, or fsmonitor off for the main checkout and on per worktree?\\\"],\\\"ruledOut\\\":[\\\"Disable fsmonitor everywhere\\\",\\\"Match daemons by command line\\\",\\\"Rely on git fsmonitor--daemon stop in a reaper\\\",\\\"Restore the reaper's daemon handling\\\"],\\\"toolsUsed\\\":[\\\"Read\\\",\\\"Grep\\\",\\\"Bash\\\"],\\\"sourcesQueried\\\":[\\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/generate-leaf-manifest.cjs:129\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs:51\\\",\\\"~/.config/git/hooks/pre-push:417\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/scripts/verify-router-sync.cjs:168\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/regenerate-skill-derived.cjs:73\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-source-tags-helper.mjs:206\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/shared/scripts/cite-drift-scan.mjs:145\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/validation/continuity-freshness.ts:38\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/scripts/lib/run-check.cjs:28\\\",\\\".skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.sh:20\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/lib/message-contract.mjs:262\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-message-gate.mjs:290\\\",\\\"rg git spawn sites under .skilled\\\",\\\"lsof socket attribution PIDs 1157,5979\\\"],\\\"edgeCase\\\":\\\"partial-success\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-10-27T09:59:59Z\\\",\\\"durationMs\\\":0,\\\"graphEvents\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"q4-call-sites\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"QUESTION\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Which git call sites lack a timeout and which should opt out of fsmonitor\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"q5-safest-default\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"QUESTION\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Safest default posture for fsmonitor and worktrees\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-hung-site-no-ceiling\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"generate-leaf-manifest.cjs:129 has no timeout and no fsmonitor opt-out\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-hook-chain\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Pre-push gate chain reaches the hung spawnSync via ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-git-no-fsmonitor-convention\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Repo already uses -c core.fsmonitor=false in six or more call sites\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-sibling-unbounded-sites\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"verify-router-sync and regenerate-skill-derived check-ignore calls are unbounded\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-timeout-precedents\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"GIT_TIMEOUT_MS and timeout:3000 are existing repo patterns\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-socket-attribution\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Main daemon identifiable by .git/fsmonitor--daemon.ipc socket path\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-default-posture\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Safest default: fsmonitor on with worktrees outside the checkout\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"edge\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"e-q4-1\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"f-hung-site-no-ceiling\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"q4-call-sites\\\",\\\"relation\\\":\\\"ANSWERS\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"edge\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"e-q4-2\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"f-hook-chain\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"f-hung-site-no-ceiling\\\",\\\"relation\\\":\\\"SUPPORTS\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"edge\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"e-q4-3\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"f-git-no-fsmonitor-convention\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"q4-call-sites\\\",\\\"relation\\\":\\\"ANSWERS\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"edge\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"e-q4-4\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"f-sibling-unbounded-sites\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"q4-call-sites\\\",\\\"relation\\\":\\\"SUPPORTS\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"edge\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"e-q4-5\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"f-timeout-precedents\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"q4-call-sites\\\",\\\"relation\\\":\\\"SUPPORTS\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"edge\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"e-q5-1\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"f-default-posture\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"q5-safest-default\\\",\\\"relation\\\":\\\"ANSWERS\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"edge\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"e-q5-2\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"f-socket-attribution\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"q5-safest-default\\\",\\\"relation\\\":\\\"SUPPORTS\\\"}]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter003-001\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The proven hung site has no ceiling and no opt-out: generate-leaf-manifest.cjs:129-133 runs spawnSync git check-ignore with no timeout option and no -c core.fsmonitor=false, and the fallback at line 136 only handles a returned failure, so a hang is never rescued.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/generate-leaf-manifest.cjs:129\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter003-002\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The pre-push hook runs ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs which imports buildManifestBytes from the manifest builder; the hook's own comment says the gate finishes in about a second, which is the assumption that failed.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"~/.config/git/hooks/pre-push:417\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/ci-skill-root-metadata.cjs:51\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter003-003\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The repository already has the fix convention: GIT_NO_FSMONITOR = ['-c','core.fsmonitor=false'] appears in cite-drift-scan.mjs, continuity-freshness.ts, check-source-tags-helper.mjs and run-check.cjs, plus git -c core.fsmonitor=false in hook-flags.sh and the QC playbook; adopting it at the hung site is the low-risk change.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/shared/scripts/cite-drift-scan.mjs:145\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/validation/continuity-freshness.ts:38\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-source-tags-helper.mjs:53\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-quality/scripts/lib/run-check.cjs:28\\\",\\\".skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.sh:20\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter003-004\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Other unbounded fsmonitor-touching call sites: verify-router-sync.cjs:168 and regenerate-skill-derived.cjs:73 run check-ignore with no opt-out and no timeout; generate-leaf-manifest.cjs:111 (rev-parse) and check-source-tags-helper.mjs:206 (opt-out present) also lack timeouts.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/scripts/verify-router-sync.cjs:168\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/regenerate-skill-derived.cjs:73\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/rules/check-source-tags-helper.mjs:206\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter003-005\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The repo does use timeouts elsewhere: message-contract.mjs wraps every git call in GIT_TIMEOUT_MS and git-message-gate.mjs uses timeout: 3000 for rev-parse, so the fix is a choice between two existing conventions.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/lib/message-contract.mjs:262\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/git-message-gate.mjs:290\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter003-006\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Roughly 59 files under .skilled spawn git; the highest-risk class is index-reading commands (check-ignore, status, ls-files) against the main checkout because those query the fsmonitor daemon; non-index commands (rev-parse, log, show, cat-file) never touch it.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"rg spawnSync/execSync/execFileSync git under .skilled (59 files)\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter003-007\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Live attribution: the main-checkout daemon holds /Users/.../Public/.git/fsmonitor--daemon.ipc (PID 5979, started 10:45:09) while worktree daemons hold a fsmonitor--daemon.ipc under their per-worktree git dirs; the socket path is the attribution key because every daemon's argv is identical.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"lsof output, this session\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter003-008\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"A fsmonitor reaper cannot use git fsmonitor--daemon stop as its escalation path because stop polls forever on exactly the wedged daemon a reaper must remove; reaping means signalling the PID directly, which contradicts the current reaper's never-signals-a-process invariant, so a fsmonitor reap belongs in a separate entry point with its own stated invariant.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\\\",\\\".skilled/bin/README.md:168\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter003-009\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Q5: the safest default is fsmonitor on with worktrees outside the checkout; it removes the trigger (the main daemon's event volume from ~2M worktree files) rather than masking it and keeps the benefit on the 570k-file main checkout, while the per-worktree opt-out requires extensions.worktreeConfig (absent today), loses the largest benefit and leaves worktree daemons free to wedge their own commands.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"git config --show-origin --get-regexp, this session\\\",\\\"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/scratch/findings.md\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter003-010\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Durability requires two changes together: set speckit.worktreeBase explicitly and stop the write-back from persisting the default as policy, otherwise the next launch without SPECKIT_WORKTREE_BASE re-pins .worktrees and the relocation silently reverts; under every option the hook ceiling is required because a wedge can still occur in any worktree.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/bin/worktree-session.sh:293\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"ruled_out\\\",\\\"direction\\\":\\\"Disable fsmonitor everywhere\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Rejected as the default rather than ruled out as an option: it discards a measured benefit on a 570k-file checkout, and per-worktree config gives the same safety with a narrower blast radius.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"ruled_out\\\",\\\"direction\\\":\\\"Match daemons by command line\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"All daemons share identical argv; the socket path is the only attribution key.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"ruled_out\\\",\\\"direction\\\":\\\"Rely on git fsmonitor--daemon stop in a reaper\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"stop polls forever on a wedged daemon, so it cannot be the escalation path by itself.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"ruled_out\\\",\\\"direction\\\":\\\"Restore the reaper's daemon handling\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The deleted code targeted MCP context-server daemons and the current reaper promises never to signal a process.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3}\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/sk-git/035-fsmonitor-daemon-and-worktree-relocation-regression/001-deep-research/research/lineages/llmgateway-flash-undated-run2/deltas/iter-003.jsonl\"}"},"time":{"start":1793095228244,"end":1793095252814}}}}
